    summary:
      'The Chinese character "首" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Head\n\nThe most common translation of "首" is "head" when referring to the top or front of something. For example:\n他的头发很乱。- His hair is very messy.\n这是一首好歌。- This is a good song.\n\n## 2. Leader\n\n"首" can also mean "leader" when referring to a person in charge or at the forefront of something. For example:\n部队的首领- The leader of the troops.\n学生会的首席- The chief of the student council.\n\n## 3. First\n\nIn certain contexts, "首" can mean "first" when indicating the beginning or primary position. For example:\n首次见面- First meeting.\n首要任务- Primary task.\n\n## 4. Measure Word\n\n"首" is also used as a measure word for music, poems, or songs, similar to "piece" in English. For example:\n两首诗- Two poems.\n一首歌曲- One song.\n\nSo in summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "首" can include "head", "leader", "first", and "measure word", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
