      'The Chinese character "灭" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Extinguish, Destroy\n\nThe most common translation of "灭" is "extinguish" or "destroy" when used to convey the idea of putting out a fire or eliminating something. For example:\n火被灭了。 - The fire was extinguished.\n敌人被消灭了。 - The enemy was destroyed.\n\n## 2. Annihilate\n\n"灭" can also mean "annihilate" or "wipe out" when describing the complete destruction of something. For example:\n摧毁一切，毫不留情，灭之而后快。 - Destroy everything without mercy, annihilate them all.\n\n## 3. Be Extinct\n\nIn certain contexts, "灭" can indicate the state of being extinct or wiped out. For example:\n这种珍稀动物面临灭绝。 - This rare animal species is facing extinction.\n\nIn summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "灭" can include "extinguish/destroy", "annihilate/wipe out", and "be extinct", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
