    summary:
      'The Chinese character "路" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Road, Path\n\nThe most common translation of "路" is "road" or "path" when referring to a route or way for traveling. For example:\n这条路很宽阔。 - This road is very wide.\n请走这条小路。 - Please take this path.\n\n## 2. Journey, Course\n\n"路" can also mean "journey" or "course" when describing a travel experience or a specific path of action. For example:\n他的人生之路很不平坦。 - His life journey is very rough.\n我们必须找到正确的发展路线。 - We must find the right course of development.\n\n## 3. Street\n\nIn some contexts, "路" can be translated as "street" when referring to a public road in a city or town. For example:\n这是一条繁华的商业街。 - This is a bustling commercial street.\n我们的公司在第三大街上。 - Our company is on Third Street.\n\nIn summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "路" can include "road/path", "journey/course", and "street", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
