    summary:
      'The Chinese character "非" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Not, Non-\n\nThe most common translation of "非" is "not" or "non-" when used to indicate negation or denial. For example:\n这不是我的手机。 - This is not my phone.\n非常 - Nonstandard\n\n## 2. Faulty, Mistaken\n\n"非" can also mean "faulty" or "mistaken" when used to indicate error or inaccuracy. For example:\n他的观点是非常错误的。 - His opinion is totally mistaken.\n非议 - Criticize\n\n## 3. Un-\n\nIn certain contexts, "非" can be used as a prefix to indicate "un-" or "non-". For example:\n非法 - Illegal\n非凡 - Extraordinary\n\n## 4. Different\n\nSometimes "非" can mean "different" or "opposite". For example:\n非黑即白 - Either black or white\n非我莫属 - None other than me\n\nSo in summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "非" can include "not/non-", "faulty/mistaken", "un-", and "different", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
