      'The Chinese character "泡" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Bubble\n\nOne common translation of "泡" is "bubble" when referring to a small, round body of gas contained in a liquid. For example:\n肥皂泡 - Soap bubble\n汽泡 - Air bubble\n\n## 2. Soak\n\n"泡" can also mean "to soak" when describing the action of immersing something in liquid for a period of time. For example:\n泡茶 - Brew tea\n泡澡 - Take a bath\n\n## 3. Flirt\n\nIn informal contexts, "泡" can be used to mean "to flirt" with someone, often in a playful or teasing manner. For example:\n他很会泡妹子。 - He\'s good at flirting with girls.\n\n## 4. Pre-soak\n\nAnother meaning of "泡" is "pre-soak", referring to the process of soaking something before further treatment. For example:\n泡面 - Instant noodles (literally means "pre-soaked noodles")\n\nSo in summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "泡" can include "bubble", "soak", "flirt", and "pre-soak", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
