      'The Arabic word "إطلا" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Spread, Expansion\n\nThe most common translation of "إطلا" is "spread" or "expansion" when referring to the act of something spreading or extending. For example:\nتمت إطلاق حملة إعلانية لنشر المعلومات. - An advertising campaign was launched to spread information.\nشهد المدينة إطلاقًا سريعًا في النمو السكاني. - The city witnessed rapid population expansion.\n\n## 2. Expanse, Range\n\n"إطلا" can also mean "expanse" or "range" when describing the extent or scope of something. For example:\nتمديد السكك الحديدية زاد من إطلاق وسائل النقل العام. - Extending the railway increased the expanse of public transportation.\nالجهاد الالكتروني يمتد إلى مختلف الإطلاقات على الإنترنت. - Cyber warfare extends to various ranges on the internet.\n\n## 3. Generosity\n\nIn certain contexts, "إطلا" can mean "generosity" when referring to a generous or open-handed attitude. For example:\nبيتنا معروف بالإطلا بالضيوف. - Our house is known for its generosity towards guests.\nأظهر الأمير إطلاقًا كبيرًا في تقديم المساعدة. - The prince showed great generosity in providing assistance.\n\n## 4. Eruption\n\nWhen used in a specific context, "إطلا" can mean "eruption" in reference to a sudden and violent ejection of something. For example:\nشهدت المنطقة إطلاقًا نشطًا للبراكين. - The region witnessed an active eruption of volcanoes.\nاندلعت الحرب بإطلاق عنيف للهجمات. - The war broke out with a violent eruption of attacks.\n\nIn summary, the English translations of the Arabic word "إطلا" can include "spread", "expansion", "expanse", "range", "generosity", and "eruption", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
