    summary:
      'The Chinese character "区" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. District, Area\n\nThe most common translation of "区" is "district" or "area" when referring to a specific geographic region or administrative division. For example:\n这个城市分为几个区？- How many districts are there in this city?\n我们住在商业区。- We live in the business district.\n\n## 2. Section, Zone\n\n"区" can also be translated as "section" or "zone" when describing a specific part or division within something. For example:\n这本书分成好几个区。- This book is divided into several sections.\n游乐园有专门的儿童区。- The amusement park has a dedicated children\'s zone.\n\n## 3. Unit\n\nIn certain contexts, "区" can mean "unit" when referring to a specialized division or department. For example:\n这是我们的财务区。- This is our finance unit.\n请到服务区办理相关手续。- Please go to the service unit to handle the relevant procedures.\n\n## 4. Quarters\n\n"区" can also refer to "quarters" when specifically talking about living quarters or residential areas. For example:\n这个基地有军事家属区。- This base has military family quarters.\n他们居住在工厂工人区。- They live in the factory workers\' quarters.\n\nIn summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "区" can include "district/area", "section/zone", "unit", and "quarters", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
