    summary:
      'The Chinese character "演" has several translations in English depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Perform\n\nThe most common translation of "演" is "perform" when referring to acting or performing. For example:\n他在电影中演了一个重要角色。 - He played an important role in the movie.\n她喜欢演戏。 - She enjoys acting.\n\n## 2. Show, Demonstrate\n\n"演" can also mean "show" or "demonstrate" when referring to displaying or presenting something. For example:\n他演示了如何操作这个软件。 - He demonstrated how to use this software.\n这个节目演得很精彩。 - The show was performed brilliantly.\n\n## 3. Rehearse\n\nIn certain contexts, "演" can mean "rehearse" when practicing for a performance or presentation. For example:\n我们需要多次演练这个节目。 - We need to rehearse this show several times.\n演一下看看效果如何。 - Let\'s rehearse and see how it goes.\n\n## 4. Engage in\n\nWhen used as a verb, "演" can also mean "to engage in" or "to participate in" an activity. For example:\n他在各种活动中积极地演着。 - He actively participates in various activities.\n她喜欢演讲和辩论比赛。 - She enjoys engaging in speeches and debates.\n\nIn summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "演" can include "perform", "show/demonstrate", "rehearse", and "engage in", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
