    summary:
      'The Chinese character "沉" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Sink, Submerge\n\nOne common translation of "沉" is "sink" or "submerge" when referring to objects or substances descending or going under a liquid surface. For example:\n这个石头沉在水里。 - This stone is sinking in the water.\n船沉没了。 - The ship has sunk.\n\n## 2. Heavy, Weighty\n\n"沉" can also mean "heavy" or "weighty" when describing the physical property of an object. For example:\n这个箱子很沉。 - This box is very heavy.\n她感到心情沉重。 - She feels emotionally heavy.\n\n## 3. Deep, Profound\n\nIn certain contexts, "沉" can be translated as "deep" or "profound" when referring to emotions, thoughts, or meanings. For example:\n他的眼睛里透露着一种深沉的忧伤。 - There is a deep sadness in his eyes.\n这个问题涉及到很深沉的哲学思考。 - This issue involves very profound philosophical thinking.\n\n## 4. Silence, Quiet\n\n"沉" can also mean "silence" or "quiet" when describing a state of being without sound or noise. For example:\n教室里陷入了沉默。 - The classroom fell into silence.\n夜晚的沉寂被突然的尖叫打破了。 - The silence of the night was broken by a sudden scream.\n\nTherefore, the English translations of the Chinese character "沉" can include "sink/submerge", "heavy/weighty", "deep/profound", and "silence/quiet", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
