      'The Chinese character "掏" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Dig out, Fish out\n\nThe most common translation of "掏" is "dig out" or "fish out" when referring to physically removing or retrieving something from a container or space. For example:\n我掏出钱包找零钱。 - I dug out my wallet to find some change.\n他掏出口袋，拿出钥匙。 - He fished out his keys from his pocket.\n\n## 2. Extort, Swindle\n\nIn certain contexts, "掏" can mean "to extort" or "to swindle" someone out of something, often in a deceitful or dishonest manner. For example:\n他被骗子掏空了银行账户。 - He was swindled and had his bank account emptied by a scammer.\n小偷趁他不注意，掏走了手机。 - The thief, taking advantage of his inattention, swindled the phone.\n\nIn summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "掏" can include "dig out", "fish out", "extort", or "swindle", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
