    summary:
      'The Chinese character "飞" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Fly\n\nThe most common translation of "飞" is "fly" when referring to movement through the air. For example:\n小鸟在天空中飞翔。 - The bird is flying in the sky.\n飞机正在飞往纽约。 - The airplane is flying to New York.\n\n## 2. Swift\n\n"飞" can also mean "swift" when describing something that moves quickly. For example:\n这匹马跑得飞快。 - This horse runs very swiftly.\n他飞快地完成了工作。 - He quickly finished the work.\n\n## 3. Soar\n\nIn certain contexts, "飞" can connote "soar" or "rise rapidly" in a majestic or powerful way. For example:\n火箭飞向太空。 - The rocket soars into space.\n梦想让我们的心灵飞翔。 - Dreams make our spirits soar.\n\n## 4. Flutter\n\nWhen used to describe small movements or actions, "飞" can mean "flutter" or "flit". For example:\n五彩的蝴蝶在花丛中飞舞。 - Colorful butterflies flutter among the flowers.\n她的思绪像蝴蝶一样飞扬。 - Her thoughts fluttered like butterflies.\n\nSo in summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "飞" can include "fly", "swift", "soar", and "flutter", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
