    summary:
      'The Persian word "شک" can have several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Doubt\n\nThe most common translation of "شک" is "doubt" when referring to uncertainty or skepticism. For example:\nاو تردید داشت. - He had doubts.\nمن بدون هیچ شک، این کار را انجام دادم. - I did this without any doubt.\n\n## 2. Suspicion\n\n"شک" can also mean "suspicion" when describing a feeling of mistrust or doubt about someone or something. For example:\nاو به من شک داشت. - He had suspicions about me.\nشک می‌کنم او دروغ می‌گوید. - I suspect he is lying.\n\n## 3. Skepticism\n\nIn certain contexts, "شک" can refer to "skepticism" which is a questioning attitude or doubt towards something. For example:\nاو به نظر من همیشه پر از شک بود. - He always seemed full of skepticism to me.\nبا شک به این موضوع نگاه کرد. - He looked at this issue with skepticism.\n\n## 4. Mistrust\n\n"شک" can also imply "mistrust" which is a lack of trust or confidence in someone or something. For example:\nما نمی‌توانیم بر او اعتماد کنیم چون شک داریم. - We can\'t trust him because we have mistrust.\nمن به او اعتماد نمی‌کنم به دلیل شک‌هایم. - I don\'t trust him because of my doubts.\n\nSo in summary, the English translations of the Persian word "شک" can include "doubt", "suspicion", "skepticism", and "mistrust", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
