    summary:
      'The Chinese character "数" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Number, Count\n\nThe most common translation of "数" is "number" or "count" when referring to quantities or figures. For example:\n这个班级有30个学生，其中数学成绩很好的有10个。 - This class has 30 students, among whom 10 excel in mathematics.\n\n## 2. To count, To calculate\n\n"数" can also mean "to count" or "to calculate" when referring to the action of determining a total or performing mathematical operations. For example:\n他在数着手上的硬币。 - He is counting the coins in his hand.\n这道数学题很难，我数了很多遍都算错。 - This math problem is difficult, I have counted many times and still got it wrong.\n\n## 3. Several, Numerous\n\nIn certain contexts, "数" can mean "several" or "numerous" when describing a large quantity or amount. For example:\n这本书有数百页。 - This book has several hundred pages.\n他获得了数个奖项。 - He has won numerous awards.\n\n## 4. Respect, Value\n\nWhen used in a more abstract or formal context, "数" can also mean "respect" or "value". For example:\n他是一位备受尊敬的老师。 - He is a teacher highly respected by all.\n这家公司被广泛认为是值得投资的。 - This company is widely regarded as a valuable investment.\n\nIn summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "数" can include "number/count", "to count/to calculate", "several/numerous", and "respect/value", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
