      'The Chinese character "棄" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Abandon\n\nThe most common translation of "棄" is "abandon" when referring to giving up, rejecting, or relinquishing something. For example:\n他棄了這個計劃。- He abandoned this plan.\n她感到被棄的失望。- She felt disappointed from being abandoned.\n\n## 2. Discard\n\n"棄" can also mean "discard" when describing throwing something away or getting rid of it. For example:\n請勿棄置垃圾。- Please do not discard trash.\n你應該棄掉這些舊衣服。- You should discard these old clothes.\n\n## 3. Give up\n\nIn certain contexts, "棄" can mean "give up" when referring to surrendering or relinquishing something. For example:\n我們不應輕易棄權。- We should not give up easily.\n他拒絕棄席而走。- He refused to give up his seat and leave.\n\n## 4. Reject\n\nWhen used as a verb, "棄" can mean "to reject" or "to refuse to accept something". For example:\n他被學校棄用。 - He was rejected by the school.\n她棄絕了他的邀請。 - She rejected his invitation.\n\nIn summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "棄" can include "abandon", "discard", "give up", and "reject", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
