    summary:
      'The Chinese character "码" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Code\n\nOne common translation of "码" is "code" when referring to a system of symbols used to represent information or instructions. For example:\n这个软件的源码很复杂。 - The source code of this software is very complex.\n请输入您的验证码。 - Please enter your verification code.\n\n## 2. Yard\n\n"码" can also mean "yard" as a unit of length, commonly used in the context of measuring textiles or fabrics. For example:\n这块布有多长? - How long is this piece of fabric?\n这家店卖的丝绸每码多少钱？- How much is this silk per yard in this shop?\n\n## 3. Number\n\nIn certain contexts, "码" can be translated as "number" when referring to a specific numerical value. For example:\n这个密码要输入几位数字？- How many numbers do I need to enter for this password?\n我家门牌号是十二号。- My house number is number twelve.\n\n## 4. Cipher\n\nSometimes "码" can also mean "cipher" in the sense of a secret or disguised way of writing. For example:\n他经常用密码保护他的文件。- He often uses ciphers to protect his files.\n\nIn summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "码" can include "code", "yard", "number", and "cipher", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
