    summary:
      'The Chinese character "如" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Like, As\n\nThe most common translation of "如" is "like" or "as" when used to make comparisons or draw similarities. For example:\n她如花一般美丽。 - She is as beautiful as a flower.\n他们如同兄弟一般。 - They are like brothers.\n\n## 2. If\n\n"如" can also mean "if" when used in conditional sentences or to express a hypothetical situation. For example:\n如果如此，我们就无法完成任务。 - If that\'s the case, we won\'t be able to complete the task.\n要是你如实告诉他，也许会有不同的结果。 - If you tell him the truth, there might be a different outcome.\n\n## 3. According to\n\nIn certain contexts, "如" can be translated as "according to" when indicating a source or reference. For example:\n如汇报显示，销售额有所增长。 - According to the report, the sales have increased.\n他们的安排如期进行。 - Their arrangements proceeded according to plan.\n\n## 4. Such as\n\n"如" can also be translated as "such as" when providing examples or listing items. For example:\n请提供一些如工作经验等相关资料。 - Please provide relevant information such as work experience and the like.\n这里有许多设施，如健身房和游泳池。 - There are many facilities here, such as a gym and a swimming pool.\n\nIn summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "如" can include "like/as", "if", "according to", and "such as", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
