    summary:
      'The Chinese character "息" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Cease, Stop\n\nThe most common translation of "息" is "cease" or "stop" when referring to actions or activities coming to an end. For example:\n停止呼吸 - Cease breathing\n不要再争吵了，让我们息事宁人吧。 - Let\'s stop arguing and make peace.\n\n## 2. Breath\n\n"息" can also mean "breath" when referring to the act of breathing or rest. For example:\n深深地呼吸一口新鲜的空气，感觉那么清新。 - Take a deep breath of fresh air, it feels so refreshing.\n夜晚的宁静只能听见他们的呼吸声息声。 - In the quiet of the night, only the sound of their breathing can be heard.\n\n## 3. Interest, Dividend\n\nIn financial contexts, "息" can mean "interest" or "dividend" when referring to financial returns or payments. For example:\n我定期获得银行利息。 - I receive interest from the bank regularly.\n这家公司今天宣布向股东分红息。 - The company announced dividend payments to shareholders today.\n\n## 4. News, Information\n\nIn certain contexts, "息" can mean "news" or "information" when referring to updates or intelligence. For example:\n他们得到了一些重要的消息，但并未公布。 - They received some important news, but did not make it public.\n警方隐瞒了这起事件的一些息。 - The police withheld some information about the incident.\n\nIn summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "息" can include "cease/stop", "breath", "interest/dividend", and "news/information", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
    sentenceId: "息",
