      'The Chinese character "换" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Change, Exchange\n\nThe most common translation of "换" is "change" or "exchange" when referring to switching or replacing something. For example:\n我们需要换一下座位。 - We need to change seats.\n我想跟你换一下手机。 - I want to exchange phones with you.\n\n## 2. Switch, Substitute\n\n"换" can also mean "switch" or "substitute" when describing replacing one thing with another. For example:\n他换了一家新公司。 - He switched to a new company.\n可以用牛奶换成豆奶吗？ - Can I substitute soy milk for regular milk?\n\n## 3. Convert, Trade\n\nIn certain contexts, "换" can mean "convert" or "trade" when referring to changing something into another form or trading goods. For example:\n这里可以换外币吗？ - Can I convert currency here?\n我想跟你换一些水果。 - I want to trade some fruit with you.\n\n## 4. Reorder, Swap\n\nWhen used as a verb, "换" can also mean "reorder" or "swap" when rearranging or exchanging items. For example:\n我想换一下这两本书的顺序。 - I want to swap the order of these two books.\n我们可以换一下时间吗？ - Can we reorder the time?\n\nSo in summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "换" can include "change/exchange", "switch/substitute", "convert/trade", and "reorder/swap", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
