    summary:
      'The Chinese character "平" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Flat, Level, Peaceful\n\nThe most common translation of "平" is "flat" or "level" when describing a surface that is even or without bumps. It can also mean "peaceful" when referring to a peaceful situation or state. For example:\n桌子很平。 - The table is very flat.\n这个地区很平静。 - This area is very peaceful.\n\n## 2. Equal, Balanced\n\n"平" can also mean "equal" or "balanced" when referring to fairness or equilibrium. For example:\n大家应该受到平等对待。 - Everyone should be treated equally.\n保持心态平衡很重要。 - It is important to maintain a balanced mindset.\n\n## 3. Common, Average\n\nIn certain contexts, "平" can mean "common" or "average" when describing something that is commonly found or of average quality. For example:\n这是一种平常的食物。 - This is a common type of food.\n他的成绩很平。 - His grades are average.\n\n## 4. Peace\n\n"平" can also mean "peace" in the sense of harmony and absence of conflict. For example:\n和平 - Peace\n\nSo in summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "平" can include "flat/level", "peaceful", "equal/balanced", "common/average", and "peace", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
