      'The Urdu word "محدود" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Limited\n\nThe most common translation of "محدود" is "limited" when referring to restrictions or boundaries. For example:\nمیرے پاس محدود وقت ہے۔ - I have limited time.\nاس کتاب کی معلومات محدود ہیں۔ - The information in this book is limited.\n\n## 2. Restricted\n\n"محدود" can also mean "restricted" when describing limited access or permissions. For example:\nسرکاری دفاتر کی سرگرمیوں میں محدودیتیں ہیں۔ - There are restrictions in government office activities.\nان کے پاس عمر میں محدودیت ہے۔ - They have age restrictions.\n\n## 3. Confined\n\nIn certain contexts, "محدود" can mean "confined" or "restricted in movement". For example:\nوہ جیل میں محدود ہوں ہیں۔ - They are confined in jail.\nمیں اس کارخانے میں محدود ہوں۔ - I am restricted in this factory.\n\n## 4. Finite\n\n"محدود" can also be translated as "finite" when referring to something having limits or boundaries. For example:\nتمام چیزیں محدود ہوتی ہیں۔ - All things are finite.\nہماری زندگی بھی محدود ہے۔ - Our life is also finite.\n\nIn summary, the English translations of the Urdu word "محدود" can include "limited", "restricted", "confined", and "finite", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
