    summary:
      'The Korean verb "버리다" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. To Throw Away\n\nThe most common translation of "버리다" is "to throw away". It is used when discarding something that is no longer needed or wanted. For example:\n종이컵을 버려야 해요. - We need to throw away the paper cup.\n이 옷은 너무 작아서 버렸어요. - I threw away this clothing because it was too small.\n\n## 2. To Abandon\n\n"버리다" can also mean "to abandon", indicating leaving something or someone behind. For example:\n고양이를 길에 버리지 마세요. - Please do not abandon cats on the street.\n그는 나를 버리고 다른 사람과 결혼했다. - He abandoned me and married someone else.\n\n## 3. To Drop\n\nIn certain contexts, "버리다" can be translated as "to drop", especially when referring to accidentally letting something fall. For example:\n휴대폰을 바닥에 버려서 깨졌어요. - I dropped my phone on the floor and it broke.\n나는 실수로 우유를 버렸어요. - I accidentally dropped the milk.\n\n## 4. To Give Up\n\nWhen used figuratively, "버리다" can mean "to give up" or "to abandon hope or efforts". For example:\n이 경기에서 이기지 못하면 우리는 모든 희망을 버렸어요. - If we don\'t win this game, we have given up all hope.\n도전하기 전에 포기하지 마세요, 그냥 내버리지 마세요. - Don’t give up before trying, don\'t just give up.\n\nIn summary, the English translations of the Korean verb "버리다" can include "to throw away", "to abandon", "to drop", and "to give up", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
