      'The Chinese character "深" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Deep\n\nThe most common translation of "深" is "deep" when referring to depth or intensity. For example:\n这个湖很深。 - This lake is very deep.\n她的爱很深。 - Her love is very deep.\n\n## 2. Profound\n\n"深" can also mean "profound" when describing something with profound significance or depth of understanding. For example:\n这位作家的作品思想很深。 - This writer\'s work is profound in thought.\n他对这个问题的见解很深。 - His understanding of this issue is profound.\n\n## 3. Dark\n\nIn certain contexts, "深" can mean "dark" when describing a dark or deep color. For example:\n这个蓝色很深。 - This blue is very dark.\n她的眼睛是深褐色的。 - Her eyes are a deep brown color.\n\n## 4. Late\n\n"深" can also mean "late" when referring to a late hour or time of day. For example:\n现在已经很深了，我们应该休息了。 - It\'s already late now, we should rest.\n他常常工作到很深的夜里。 - He often works until late at night.\n\nIn summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "深" can include "deep", "profound", "dark", and "late", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
