    summary:
      'The Chinese character "传" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Transmit, Pass On\n\nThe most common translation of "传" is "transmit" or "pass on", especially when referring to information, knowledge, or traditions. For example:\n这个消息需要传达给所有员工。 - This message needs to be conveyed to all employees.\n他们代代相传这个传统。 - They have passed down this tradition from generation to generation.\n\n## 2. Biography, Story\n\n"传" can also mean "biography" or "story" when referring to a written or oral account of someone\'s life or events. For example:\n这本书是他的传记。 - This book is his biography.\n这个传说讲述了一个美丽的故事。 - This legend tells a beautiful story.\n\n## 3. Spread, Circulate\n\nIn certain contexts, "传" can mean "spread" or "circulate", especially in relation to news or rumors. For example:\n这个消息已经传遍了整个城市。 - This news has spread throughout the entire city.\n谣言很快就传播开来了。 - The rumor quickly circulated.\n\n## 4. Inherit, Hand Down\n\nWhen used in the context of inheritance or passing down traditions, "传" can mean "inherit" or "hand down". For example:\n这个家族的企业将由他的儿子传承。 - The family business will be inherited by his son.\n他们将家族文化传给下一代。 - They will pass down the family culture to the next generation.\n\nIn summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "传" can include "transmit/pass on", "biography/story", "spread/circulate", and "inherit/hand down", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
