      'The Persian word "الکل" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Alcohol\n\nThe most common translation of "الکل" is "alcohol" when referring to the substance used in beverages and chemicals. For example:\nاین نوشیدنی حاوی الکل است. - This beverage contains alcohol.\nالکل مقدار زیادی در تمیزی و ضدعفونی کردن استفاده می‌شود. - Alcohol is used in large amounts for cleaning and disinfecting.\n\n## 2. Spirit\n\n"الکل" can also mean "spirit" in a more abstract or metaphorical sense, such as expressing courage or vigor. For example:\nاو دارای روحیه‌ی الکلی بالاست. - He has a high spirit.\nبا این تلاش و الکلیت، می‌توانیم به اهدافمان برسیم. - With this effort and spirit, we can achieve our goals.\n\n## 3. Pure\n\nIn specific contexts, "الکل" can mean "pure" or "absolute", indicating a high level of quality or concentration. For example:\nاین آب الکلی بسیار پاکیزه است. - This alcohol is very pure.\nتنها الکل در این محصول استفاده شده است. - Only pure alcohol is used in this product.\n\n## 4. Essence\n\nSometimes, "الکل" can also refer to "essence" or "extract", highlighting the primary or concentrated form of something. For example:\nعطر الکل یکی از مؤلفه‌های اصلی این عطر است. - Alcohol essence is one of the main components of this perfume.\nاین دارو الکلی برای ضدعفونی کردن پوست مناسب است. - This alcohol extract is suitable for disinfecting the skin.\n\nIn summary, the English translations of the Persian word "الکل" can include "alcohol", "spirit", "pure", and "essence", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
