    summary:
      'The Chinese character "体现" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Reflect, Manifest\n\nThe most common translation of "体现" is "reflect" or "manifest" when referring to the expression or embodiment of something. For example:\n这部电影体现了友谊的力量。 - This movie reflects the power of friendship.\n他的作品体现了他的独特风格。 - His work manifests his unique style.\n\n## 2. Showcase, Demonstrate\n\n"体现" can also mean "showcase" or "demonstrate" when describing the display or presentation of something. For example:\n这次展览体现了当代艺术的多样性。 - This exhibition showcases the diversity of contemporary art.\n她的演技体现了她的才华。 - Her acting demonstrates her talent.\n\n## 3. Represent, Embody\n\nIn certain contexts, "体现" can mean "represent" or "embody" when referring to the representation or embodiment of an idea or quality. For example:\n这个决定体现了公司的价值观。 - This decision represents the values of the company.\n他的行动体现了勇气和决心。 - His actions embody courage and determination.\n\n## 4. Reflect, Realize\n\nWhen used as a verb, "体现" can also translate to "reflect" or "realize" when describing the realization or recognition of something. For example:\n这个方案体现了我们的努力得到了回报。 - This plan reflects that our efforts have paid off.\n这一时刻体现了他们的爱情。 - This moment realizes their love.\n\nSo in summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "体现" can include "reflect", "manifest", "showcase", "demonstrate", "represent", "embody", and "realize", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
