    summary:
      'The Chinese character "通" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Pass through, Communicate\n\nThe most common translation of "通" is "pass through" or "communicate" when referring to movement or information exchange. For example:\n这条道路通向市中心。 - This road leads to the city center.\n我们可以通过邮件通知客户。 - We can communicate with customers through email.\n\n## 2. Understand, Unobstructed\n\n"通" can also mean "understand" or "unobstructed" when describing comprehension or pathways. For example:\n我听不懂他在说什么，他的话太通俗了。 - I don\'t understand what he\'s saying, his words are too colloquial.\n电话线路通畅。 - The phone lines are unobstructed.\n\n## 3. Connect, General\n\nIn certain contexts, "通" can mean "connect" or "general" when referring to connections or in a broad sense. For example:\n这个城市的地铁系统连接了各个主要区域。 - The subway system of this city connects all major areas.\n这是通用的规定。 - This is a general rule.\n\n## 4. Penetrate, Thoroughfare\n\nWhen used in a more specific context, "通" can mean "to penetrate" or "thoroughfare". For example:\n他的眼神透过我的谎言，看穿了我的内心。 - His eyes penetrated through my lies and saw through my heart.\n这条街是市中心的主要通道。 - This street is the main thoroughfare of the city center.\n\nSo in summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "通" can include "pass through/communicate", "understand/unobstructed", "connect/general", and "penetrate/thoroughfare", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
