      'The Persian word "نام" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Name\n\nThe most common translation of "نام" is "name" when referring to the label by which a person, animal, place, or thing is identified. For example:\nنام من سارا است. - My name is Sara.\nاین مکان نام آن تاور است. - This place is called An Tower.\n\n## 2. Reputation, Honor\n\n"نام" can also mean "reputation" or "honor" when describing a person\'s character or standing in society. For example:\nاو نام خانواده‌اش را حفظ کرد. - He upheld his family\'s reputation.\nاو نام خانواده خود را ساده نگاه کرد. - She brought honor to her family.\n\n## 3. Title\n\nIn certain contexts, "نام" can refer to a title or designation. For example:\n"دکتر" یکی از نام‌های اوست. - "Doctor" is one of his titles.\nآیه‌ای به نام "توحید" بشنوید. - Listen to a verse called "Tawhid".\n\n## 4. Fame\n\n"نام" can also mean "fame" or "celebrity" in the sense of being widely recognized and acclaimed. For example:\nاو به روزی رسید که نامش به رقابت می‌آمد. - The day came when his fame was challenged.\nلوئیس آرمسترانگ یکی از نام‌های پرافتخار جاز است. - Louis Armstrong is a famous name in jazz.\n\nTherefore, the English translations of the Persian word "نام" can include "name", "reputation/honor", "title", and "fame", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
