    summary:
      'The Chinese character "代" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Generation, Era\n\nOne common translation of "代" is "generation" or "era" when referring to a specific time period or group of people. For example:\n这是我们这个代人的责任。 - This is the responsibility of our generation.\n这是一个新时代的开始。 - This marks the beginning of a new era.\n\n## 2. Substitute, Replacement\n\n"代" can also mean "substitute" or "replacement" when describing someone or something taking the place of another. For example:\n他是我的代班同事。 - He is my substitute colleague.\n这部手机是上一代的产品。 - This phone is a product from the previous generation.\n\n## 3. Agency, Representative\n\nIn certain contexts, "代" can refer to an "agency" or "representative" acting on behalf of someone else. For example:\n我们派了代表去参加会议。 - We sent representatives to attend the meeting.\n你可以找我们的代理商购买产品。 - You can buy the products from our agency.\n\n## 4. Success, Inheritance\n\nAnother meaning of "代" is "success" or "inheritance" when referring to passing down traditions, values, or responsibilities. For example:\n他将来会继承家族的产业。 - He will inherit the family business in the future.\n这部电影是经典作品的传承代表。 - This movie represents the inheritance of classic works.\n\nIn summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "代" can include "generation/era", "substitute/replacement", "agency/representative", and "success/inheritance", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
