    summary:
      'The Chinese character "到" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Arrive\n\nThe most common translation of "到" is "arrive" when referring to reaching a destination. For example:\n他终于到家了。 - He finally arrived home.\n我们什么时候到达机场？ - When will we arrive at the airport?\n\n## 2. To\n\n"到" can also mean "to" when indicating a direction or destination. For example:\n我要走到学校。 - I am walking to the school.\n他去到哪里了？ - Where did he go to?\n\n## 3. Reach\n\nIn certain contexts, "到" can be translated as "reach" when describing achieving a goal or destination. For example:\n目标终于达到了！ - The goal has finally been reached!\n他们漫长的旅程终于到了尽头。 - Their long journey finally reached its end.\n\n## 4. Up to\n\nWhen used with quantities or amounts, "到" can indicate "up to" or "until". For example:\n这件外套打了五折，最多到120元。 - This coat is on sale at 50% off, up to a maximum of 120 yuan.\n他们工作到深夜。 - They worked until late at night.\n\nIn summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "到" can include "arrive", "to", "reach", and "up to", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
