      'The Urdu word "اِنصاف" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Justice\n\nThe most common translation of "اِنصاف" is "justice" when referring to fairness, righteousness, or the legal system. For example:\nانصاف کی بات ہے کہ ہر انسان کو برابر موازنہ میں اپنا حق ملے۔ - Justice demands that every individual receives their rights equally.\n\n## 2. Fairness\n\n"اِنصاف" can also mean "fairness" when describing equitable treatment or impartiality. For example:\nاداکار نے بتایا کہ اُنہیں کریکٹ کے اُمیدواروں کا انصاف ملنا چاہیے۔ - The actor said that cricket aspirants should receive fairness.\n\n## 3. Judgment\n\nIn certain contexts, "اِنصاف" can mean "judgment" when referring to decisions or opinions. For example:\nاس الفاظ کا انتہا پر انصاف کریں۔ - Exercise judgment at the end of these words.\n\n## 4. Rectitude\n\n"اِنصاف" can also be translated as "rectitude" which implies moral integrity or correctness. For example:\nوہ شخص انصاف اور صداقت کے پیچھے پرے ہوتا ہے۔ - He is a person inclined towards justice and honesty.\n\nSo in summary, the English translations of the Urdu word "اِنصاف" can include "justice", "fairness", "judgment", and "rectitude", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
