    summary:
      'The Chinese character "便利" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Convenient\n\nThe most common translation of "便利" is "convenient" when referring to something that is easy to use or helpful. For example:\n这家便利店离我家很近。 - This convenience store is very close to my house.\n这个应用程序非常便利。 - This app is very convenient.\n\n## 2. Facility\n\n"便利" can also mean "facility" when describing a public amenity or service that provides convenience. For example:\n这个健身房的设施非常齐全，很便利。 - This gym has great facilities, very convenient.\n这个商场的停车设施很便利。 - The parking facilities at this mall are very convenient.\n\n## 3. Handy\n\nIn certain contexts, "便利" can be translated as "handy" when describing something that is useful or easy to handle. For example:\n这个小工具非常便利。 - This small tool is very handy.\n这种便利食品非常方便。 - These handy convenience foods are very convenient.\n\n## 4. Expedient\n\n"便利" can also mean "expedient" when referring to something that is advantageous or beneficial. For example:\n这个方案很便利解决了我们的问题。 - This solution expediently solved our problem.\n利用这种方法是最便利的。 - Using this method is the most expedient.\n\nIn summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "便利" can include "convenient", "facility", "handy", and "expedient", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
