    summary:
      'The Chinese character "放" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Release, Put\n\nThe most common translation of "放" is "release" or "put" when referring to actions such as letting go or placing something somewhere. For example:\n放开我的手！ - Let go of my hand!\n把书放在桌子上。 - Put the book on the table.\n\n## 2. Let Go, Set Free\n\n"放" can also mean "let go" or "set free" when describing the act of releasing something or someone. For example:\n放风筝 - Fly a kite (literally: release a kite)\n把鱼放回水里。 - Put the fish back in the water (set the fish free).\n\n## 3. Show, Broadcast\n\nIn certain contexts, "放" can mean "show" or "broadcast" when referring to displaying or airing something. For example:\n放映电影 - Show a movie\n电视台放送了一场新闻节目。 - The TV station broadcasted a news program.\n\n## 4. Relax, Let Be\n\n"放" can also mean "relax" or "let be" when describing a state of ease or letting things take their course. For example:\n放心 - Relax (literally: put your heart/mind at ease)\n随它去吧，别想太多。 - Just let it be, don\'t overthink it.\n\nIn summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "放" can include "release/put", "let go/set free", "show/broadcast", and "relax/let be", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
