    createdAt: 1712283119220,
    summary:
      'The Chinese phrase "差不多" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Almost, Nearly\n\nThe most common translation of "差不多" is "almost" or "nearly" when referring to a close approximation or similarity. For example:\n我们的工作进展差不多了。 - Our work progress is almost done.\n这两个电影的长度差不多。 - The lengths of these two movies are nearly the same.\n\n## 2. About the Same, Similar\n\n"差不多" can also mean "about the same" or "similar" when comparing things that are alike. For example:\n这两个口味的冰淇淋味道差不多。 - The tastes of these two ice cream flavors are about the same.\n他们的观点差不多。 - Their viewpoints are similar.\n\n## 3. Good Enough, Passable\n\nIn certain contexts, "差不多" can mean "good enough" or "passable" when referring to quality or standard. For example:\n这个答案差不多了。 - This answer is good enough.\n这种方法差不多能用。 - This method is passable and can be used.\n\n## 4. Close, Nearby\n\n"差不多" can also mean "close" or "nearby" when describing proximity. For example:\n公司就在差不多的地方。 - The company is located close by.\n学校离这里差不多五分钟的路程。 - The school is about five minutes away from here.\n\nSo in summary, the English translations of the Chinese phrase "差不多" can include "almost/nearly", "about the same/similar", "good enough/passable", and "close/nearby", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
    sentenceId: "差不多",
    creator: "learnuidev@gmail.com",
