      'The Persian word "زندگی" has multiple translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Life\n\nThe most common translation of "زندگی" is "life", referring to the state of being alive or the existence of a living organism. For example:\nاو زندگی خوبی دارد. - He has a good life.\nزندگی چگونه است؟ - How is life?\n\n## 2. Living\n\n"زندگی" can also mean "living" when describing the act of being alive or the experience of life itself. For example:\nیادگیری یک فرآیند زندگی است. - Learning is a process of living.\nهنر به زندگی ارزش می افزاید. - Art adds value to living.\n\n## 3. Livelihood\n\nIn certain contexts, "زندگی" can refer to "livelihood" or the means of making a living. For example:\nکشاورزی معیشت زندگی اکثر مردم این روستاست. - Agriculture is the livelihood of most people in this village.\nبا مشکلات اقتصادی، زندگی سخت است. - With economic difficulties, livelihood is hard.\n\n## 4. Biography\n\n"زندگی" can also mean "biography" when referring to the story of someone\'s life or their life history. For example:\nاین کتاب زندگینامه یک نویسنده معروف است. - This book is the biography of a famous writer.\nاو زندگینامه خواندنی‌ای دارد. - He has an interesting biography.\n\nIn summary, the English translations of the Persian word "زندگی" can include "life", "living", "livelihood", and "biography", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
