    summary:
      'The Chinese term "接待" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Receive, Welcome\n\n"接待" can be translated as "receive" or "welcome" when referring to receiving or welcoming guests, visitors, or clients. For example:\n我们公司的接待员非常热情。 - The receptionist at our company is very welcoming.\n这里有专门的接待处。 - There is a dedicated reception area here.\n\n## 2. Host, Entertain\n\nIn certain contexts, "接待" can mean "host" or "entertain" when referring to hosting or entertaining guests or visitors. For example:\n公司总经理亲自接待了客户。 - The company\'s general manager personally hosted the clients.\n他们接待了一群外国游客。 - They entertained a group of foreign tourists.\n\nIn summary, the English translations of the Chinese term "接待" can include "receive", "welcome", "host", and "entertain", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
