    summary:
      'The Chinese character "说" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Speak, Say\n\nThe most common translation of "说" is "speak" or "say" when referring to verbal communication. For example:\n他说中文。 - He speaks Chinese.\n她说了一些重要的事情。 - She said some important things.\n\n## 2. Talk, Tell\n\n"说" can also mean "talk" or "tell" when describing communication or narration. For example:\n我们需要好好谈一谈。 - We need to have a good talk.\n请告诉我真相。 - Please tell me the truth.\n\n## 3. Explain\n\nIn certain contexts, "说" can mean "explain" when clarifying or providing details. For example:\n我不会解释得更清楚了。 - I can\'t explain it any clearer.\n他说了原因。 - He explained the reasons.\n\n## 4. Promise\n\n"说" can also mean "promise" when making a commitment or assurance. For example:\n你说过会帮我的。 - You promised to help me.\n他说了要好好学习。 - He promised to study hard.\n\nSo in summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "说" can include "speak/say", "talk/tell", "explain", and "promise", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
