    summary:
      'The Chinese character "宽" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Wide\n\nThe most common translation of "宽" is "wide" when referring to the width or breadth of something. For example:\n这条路很宽。 - This road is very wide.\n这幅画的框架很宽。 - The frame of this painting is very wide.\n\n## 2. Broad, Spacious\n\n"宽" can also mean "broad" or "spacious" when describing an area or space. For example:\n这个房间很宽敞。 - This room is very spacious.\n这座广场很宽阔。 - This square is very broad.\n\n## 3. Lenient\n\nIn certain contexts, "宽" can mean "lenient" when describing a person\'s attitude or a rule. For example:\n他对待员工很宽容。 - He is very lenient towards his employees.\n学校对迟到的规定很宽松。 - The school has very lenient rules for lateness.\n\n## 4. Wide-ranging, Extensive\n\nWhen used in a metaphorical sense, "宽" can also mean "wide-ranging" or "extensive". For example:\n他的知识面很宽。 - His knowledge is extensive.\n这家公司的业务范围很宽广。 - This company has a wide-ranging scope of business.\n\nSo in summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "宽" can include "wide", "broad/spacious", "lenient", and "wide-ranging/extensive", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
