      'The Portuguese word "instaurar" can be translated into English as "establish," "institute," or "restore," depending on the context in which it is used.\n\n## 1. Establish\n\n"Instaurar" can be translated as "establish" when referring to setting up or creating something new. For example:\n- O objetivo era instaurar um novo sistema de ensino. (The goal was to establish a new education system.)\n\n## 2. Institute\n\n"Instaurar" can also be translated as "institute" when referring to officially introducing or implementing something. For example:\n- As autoridades decidiram instaurar novas medidas de segurança. (The authorities decided to institute new security measures.)\n\n## 3. Restore\n\nIn some contexts, "instaurar" can mean "restore" when referring to bringing back or reestablishing something. For example:\n- O programa visa instaurar a paz na região. (The program aims to restore peace in the region.)\n\nTherefore, the English translations of the Portuguese word "instaurar" include "establish," "institute," and "restore," depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
