    summary:
      'The Chinese character "壮" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Strong, Robust\n\nThe most common translation of "壮" is "strong" or "robust" when describing physical strength or health. For example:\n他的身体很壮实。 - His body is very strong.\n他是一个壮硕的运动员。 - He is a robust athlete.\n\n## 2. Magnificent, Grand\n\n"壮" can also mean "magnificent" or "grand" when describing something impressive or majestic. For example:\n这座大桥确实很壮观。 - This bridge is truly magnificent.\n壮丽的风景吸引了许多游客。 - The grand scenery attracts many tourists.\n\n## 3. Flourish, Thrive\n\nIn certain contexts, "壮" can mean "to flourish" or "to thrive", indicating prosperity or growth. For example:\n这个城市的经济发展得很壮。 - The city\'s economy is flourishing.\n作物在这块土地上生长得很壮。 - The crops thrive on this land.\n\n## 4. Manly, Heroic\n\n"壮" can also convey the meaning of "manly" or "heroic" when describing someone brave or strong-willed. For example:\n他展现出了壮丽的气概。 - He displayed a heroic spirit.\n壮士断腕 - A heroic act of self-sacrifice\n\nOverall, the English translations of the Chinese character "壮" can include "strong/robust", "magnificent/grand", "flourish/thrive", and "manly/heroic", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
