      'The Chinese character "填" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Fill\n\nThe most common translation of "填" is "fill" when referring to filling something up or completing a form. For example:\n请填写您的姓名。- Please fill in your name.\n这个杯子里填满了水。- This cup is filled with water.\n\n## 2. Stuff\n\n"填" can also mean "stuff" when describing filling something with material or substance. For example:\n这个玩具填满了棉花。- This toy is stuffed with cotton.\n\n## 3. Seal\n\nIn certain contexts, "填" can mean "seal" when referring to sealing or closing a gap or hole. For example:\n请用胶水把这个缝隙填起来。- Please seal this gap with glue.\n他填好了树洞，以防止小动物进入。- He sealed up the tree hole to prevent small animals from entering.\n\n## 4. Complete\n\nWhen used as a verb, "填" can mean "to complete" or "to fill out". For example:\n请填写完整的地址。- Please fill out the complete address.\n她填好了报名表格。- She completed the registration form.\n\nSo in summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "填" can include "fill", "stuff", "seal", and "complete", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
