    summary:
      'The Chinese character "复" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Repeat, Duplicate\n\nThe most common translation of "复" is "repeat" or "duplicate" when referring to doing something again or creating a copy. For example:\n请复制并粘贴这段文字。- Please copy and paste this text.\n这个动作需要复述两次。- This action needs to be repeated twice.\n\n## 2. Reply, Respond\n\n"复" can also mean "reply" or "respond" in the context of communication or answering someone. For example:\n他还没有复我。- He hasn\'t replied to me yet.\n请在两天内复我。- Please respond to me within two days.\n\n## 3. Resume, Restore\n\nIn certain contexts, "复" can mean "resume" or "restore" when referring to continuing or returning something to its original state. For example:\n恢复 - resume\n复原 - restore\n\n## 4. Complex, Compound\n\n"复" can also mean "complex" or "compound" when describing something composed of multiple parts or elements. For example:\n复杂 - complex\n复合 - compound\n\nSo in summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "复" can include "repeat/duplicate", "reply/respond", "resume/restore", and "complex/compound", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
