    summary:
      'The Chinese character "照" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Shine, Illuminate\n\nThe most common translation of "照" is "shine" or "illuminate" when referring to light or brightness. For example:\n太阳照得很明亮。 - The sun is shining very brightly.\n请把灯照到这个角落。 - Please shine the light on this corner.\n\n## 2. Take a Photo\n\n"照" can also mean "take a photo" or "take a picture" when referring to capturing an image. For example:\n我们在海边照了很多照片。 - We took a lot of photos at the beach.\n她喜欢照自拍。 - She likes taking selfies.\n\n## 3. According to, In accordance with\n\nIn certain contexts, "照" can mean "according to" or "in accordance with" when describing following rules or standards. For example:\n照规定完成任务。 - Complete the task according to the regulations.\n照公司政策办事。 - Handle things in accordance with the company\'s policies.\n\n## 4. Reflect\n\n"照" can also mean "reflect" when referring to mirroring or reflecting back. For example:\n镜子照出了她的影子。- The mirror reflected her image.\n水面照出了月亮的倒影。 - The water surface reflected the moon\'s image.\n\nIn summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "照" can include "shine/illuminate", "take a photo", "according to/in accordance with", and "reflect", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
