      'The Chinese character "补" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Mend, Repair\n\nThe most common translation of "补" is "mend" or "repair" when referring to fixing something that is damaged or broken. For example:\n她会补裤子。 - She can mend pants.\n需要补一下这个漏洞。 - This hole needs to be repaired.\n\n## 2. Supplement\n\n"补" can also mean "supplement" when referring to adding something extra to make up for a deficiency. For example:\n吃点维生素来补充营养。 - Take some vitamins to supplement nutrients.\n这些资料没有完整，需要补充。 - These documents are not complete, they need to be supplemented.\n\n## 3. Apply, Patch\n\nIn some contexts, "补" can be translated as "apply" or "patch" when referring to covering up or filling in something. For example:\n补一下创口。 - Apply a patch to the wound.\n这块地方需要补漆。 - This area needs to be patched up with paint.\n\n## 4. Fill\n\nWhen used as a verb, "补" can mean "to fill" or "to make something whole or complete". For example:\n她的笑容补满了他的心。 - Her smile filled his heart.\n这个空缺需要马上补上。 - This vacancy needs to be filled immediately.\n\nIn summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "补" can include "mend/repair", "supplement", "apply/patch", and "fill", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
