    summary:
      'The Chinese character "过" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Pass\n\nOne of the main translations of "过" is "pass", often used to indicate passing through a location, a period of time, or a test. For example:\n他经过这个街道。 - He passed through this street.\n考试过了吗？ - Did you pass the exam?\n\n## 2. Cross\n\n"过" can also mean "cross" when referring to crossing a road, a river, or any other physical barrier. For example:\n过马路 - Cross the road\n过河 - Cross the river\n\n## 3. Excessive\n\nIn certain contexts, "过" can convey the meaning of "excessive" or "too much". For example:\n你吃得太过了！ - You ate too much!\n这个问题过于复杂。 - This problem is too complicated.\n\n## 4. Experience\n\n"过" can also mean "experience", denoting the experience of going through something. For example:\n他有过很多困难。 - He has experienced a lot of difficulties.\n这是我第一次过生日。 - This is my first birthday celebration.\n\nIn summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "过" can include "pass", "cross", "excessive", and "experience", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
