      'The Chinese character "岩" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Rock\n\nThe most common translation of "岩" is "rock" when referring to solid mineral material. For example:\n这座山上有很多岩石。- This mountain has a lot of rocks.\n这座桥的基础是用岩石建造的。- The foundation of this bridge is built with rocks.\n\n## 2. Cliff \n\n"岩" can also mean "cliff" when describing a steep rock face or escarpment. For example:\n他站在悬崖上看风景。- He stood on the cliff to admire the view.\n这座岩壁很陡峭。- This cliff is very steep.\n\n## 3. Cave \n\nIn certain contexts, "岩" can mean "cave" when referring to a natural underground space. For example:\n这座山里有许多美丽的岩洞。- This mountain has many beautiful caves.\n我们在岩洞中发现了史前壁画。- We found prehistoric cave paintings in the cave.\n\n## 4. Granite \n\n"岩" can also refer to "granite," a type of hard, granular, crystalline rock commonly found in the earth\'s crust. For example:\n这座岛上的建筑材料主要是由岩石制成的。- The construction materials on this island are mainly made of granite.\n许多雕刻作品都是用岩石雕刻而成的。- Many sculptures are carved from granite.\n\nIn summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "岩" can include "rock," "cliff," "cave," and "granite," depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
