    summary:
      'The Chinese character "留" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Stay, Remain\n\nThe most common translation of "留" is "stay" or "remain" when referring to someone staying in a place or something being left behind. For example:\n他留在家里不出门。 - He stays at home and doesn\'t go out.\n请留下你的姓名和联系方式。 - Please leave your name and contact information.\n\n## 2. Keep, Retain\n\n"留" can also mean "keep" or "retain" when indicating the act of preserving something. For example:\n留住这美好的记忆。 - Keep/retain this beautiful memory.\n这些照片让我想要留着它们。 - These photos make me want to keep them.\n\n## 3. Await, Expect\n\nIn certain contexts, "留" can mean "await" or "expect" when describing waiting for someone or something. For example:\n请留意最新消息更新。 - Please await/expect the latest news updates.\n她留意着他的到来。 - She waited/expected his arrival.\n\n## 4. Record, Leave a Message\n\nSometimes, "留" can be translated as "record" or "leave a message" in the context of writing something down or leaving a note. For example:\n留言后，我们会尽快回复您。 - After leaving a message, we will reply to you as soon as possible.\n请留下您的建议。 - Please leave your suggestions.\n\nOverall, the English translations of the Chinese character "留" can include "stay/remain", "keep/retain", "await/expect", and "record/leave a message", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
