    summary:
      'The Chinese character "度" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Degree, Degree Celsius\n\nOne common translation of "度" is "degree", especially when referring to temperature measurements in Celsius. For example:\n今天气温是三十度。- Today\'s temperature is 30 degrees.\n这个房间有点冷，大概只有十度。- This room is a bit cold, probably only 10 degrees.\n\n## 2. Measure, Measurement\n\n"度" can also mean "measure" or "measurement" when used in contexts related to quantifying or evaluating something. For example:\n这家餐馆的服务水平很高，值得五星好评。- This restaurant\'s service level is very high, deserving a five-star rating.\n他的成功不能仅仅用金钱来度量。- His success cannot be measured solely by money.\n\n## 3. To Handle, To Deal With\n\nIn certain contexts, "度" can mean "to handle" or "to deal with" a situation or problem. For example:\n他喜欢用平和的心态来度过生活中的困难。- He likes to deal with life\'s difficulties with a calm attitude.\n这个问题需要采取一种更加有效的方法来度。- This problem needs to be dealt with in a more effective way.\n\n## 4. Degree, Extent\n\n"度" can also denote "degree" or "extent" in expressions that convey a certain level or extent of something. For example:\n他的病情已经恶化到了不可逆的度数。- His condition has deteriorated to an irreversible extent.\n我们对这个问题的了解程度还不够。- Our understanding of this issue is not sufficient.\n\nIn summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "度" can include "degree", "measure/measurement", "to handle/to deal with", and "degree/extent", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
