      'The Chinese character "遥" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Distant\n\nThe most common translation of "遥" is "distant" when referring to faraway locations or relationships. For example:\n他们之间的距离很遥远。- The distance between them is very distant.\n遥远的星系 - Distant galaxy\n\n## 2. Remote\n\n"遥" can also mean "remote" when describing something that is far away or isolated. For example:\n这个地方很遥远。- This place is very remote.\n遥远的山区 - Remote mountainous region\n\n## 3. Far\n\nIn certain contexts, "遥" can simply mean "far" or "far away". For example:\n目标还很遥远。- The goal is still far away.\n遥遥无期 - Far off into the future\n\n## 4. Indistinct\n\nSometimes, "遥" can also mean "indistinct" when referring to something that is unclear or not easy to perceive. For example:\n远处的灯光显得很遥。- The light in the distance appears indistinct.\n远山被迷雾所遮盖，若隐若现，遥远而亲近。- The distant mountains are covered by mist, appearing indistinct, distant, and yet close.\n\nSo in summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "遥" can include "distant", "remote", "far", and "indistinct", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
