      'The Chinese character "暑" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Hot Summer\n\nThe most common translation of "暑" is "hot summer" when referring to the season of summer and the heat that comes with it. For example:\n今年的暑天特别炎热。 - This year\'s hot summer days are especially scorching.\n暑假是孩子们最喜欢的假期之一。 - Summer vacation is one of the children\'s favorite holidays.\n\n## 2. Hot\n\n"暑" can also mean "hot" when describing the temperature or weather. For example:\n今天真是暑热难耐。 - Today is unbearably hot.\n炎炎暑日让人感到疲惫。 - The scorching hot days make people feel tired.\n\n## 3. Heat\n\nIn certain contexts, "暑" can refer specifically to "heat" or "hot weather". For example:\n今年夏天的暑气异常。 - The heat this summer is extraordinary.\n暑期高温会对农作物产生影响。 - High temperatures during the summer will affect crops.\n\nSo in summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "暑" can include "hot summer", "hot", and "heat", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
