    summary:
      'The Chinese character "议" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Discuss, Debate\n\nThe most common translation of "议" is "discuss" or "debate" when referring to conversations or deliberations. For example:\n我们需要开会议讨论这个问题。 - We need to have a meeting to discuss this issue.\n他们正在议论如何解决这个困难。 - They are debating how to solve this difficulty.\n\n## 2. Proposal\n\n"议" can also mean "proposal" when suggesting an idea or plan. For example:\n提出了一个新的议案。 - Put forward a new proposal.\n通过了这项议案。 - Passed this proposal.\n\n## 3. Consultation\n\nIn certain contexts, "议" can refer to "consultation" when seeking advice or opinions. For example:\n进行了专家们的建议性议。 - Conducted a consultative meeting with experts.\n请给我们提供您的意见和建议。 - Please provide us with your opinions and suggestions.\n\n## 4. Assembly, Meeting\n\n"议" can also mean "assembly" or "meeting" in the sense of a formal gathering. For example:\n全体议通过了这项决议。 - The assembly passed this resolution.\n参加了一次重要的议。 - Attended an important meeting.\n\nIn summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "议" can include "discuss/debate", "proposal", "consultation", and "assembly/meeting", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
