    summary:
      'The Chinese character "曰" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Say, Speak\n\nOne common translation of "曰" is "say" or "speak" when referring to verbal communication. For example:\n他曰：“你好！” - He said, "Hello!"\n她曰：“谢谢！” - She spoke, "Thank you!"\n\n## 2. Call, Name\n\n"曰" can also mean "call" or "name" when referring to identifying or addressing someone or something. For example:\n他曰我为“朋友”。 - He called me "friend".\n这家店曰“快乐小店”。 - This store is named "Happy Mart".\n\n## 3. That, Thus\n\nIn certain contexts, "曰" can be translated as "that" or "thus" when expressing a statement or fact. For example:\n曰有此物。 - Thus, this item exists.\n\nSo in summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "曰" can include "say/speak", "call/name", and "that/thus", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
