    summary:
      'The Chinese character "差" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Difference, Discrepancy\n\nOne common translation of "差" is "difference" or "discrepancy" when referring to a gap or distinction between things. For example:\n这两个数之间有很大的差别。 - There is a big difference between these two numbers.\n我们之间存在一些差异。 - There are some discrepancies between us.\n\n## 2. Lack, Shortage\n\n"差" can also mean "lack" or "shortage" when describing a deficiency or insufficiency of something. For example:\n这家店的服务态度有些差。 - The service attitude of this store is a bit lacking.\n他的表现差了一些。 - His performance has been lacking lately.\n\n## 3. Deviation, Deviate\n\nIn certain contexts, "差" can indicate "deviation" or "to deviate" from a standard or expected behavior. For example:\n他偏差了原本的计划。 - He deviated from the original plan.\n这个结果与预期有一定的差距。 - There is a certain deviation from the expected result.\n\n## 4. Dispatch\n\nAnother translation of "差" is "dispatch" when used in the context of sending someone or something. For example:\n我已经差人去取包裹了。 - I have dispatched someone to pick up the parcel.\n\nIn summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "差" can include "difference/discrepancy", "lack/shortage", "deviation/deviate", and "dispatch", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
