    summary:
      'The Chinese character "相反" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Opposite\n\nThe most common translation of "相反" is "opposite" when referring to something being contrary or diametrically opposed. For example:\n这两个观点完全相反。 - These two views are completely opposite.\n他们的性格是相反的。 - Their personalities are opposite.\n\n## 2. Contrary\n\n"相反" can also mean "contrary" when describing something that is different or opposed to another. For example:\n我的意见和他的相反。 - My opinion is contrary to his.\n他的行为常常与他的言论相反。 - His actions are often contrary to his words.\n\n## 3. Inverse\n\nIn certain contexts, "相反" can be translated as "inverse" when referring to a relationship that is the opposite or reverse of another. For example:\n这两个数字是相反数。 - These two numbers are inverses of each other.\n黑色和白色是相反的颜色。 - Black and white are inverse colors.\n\n## 4. Contradictory\n\nWhen used to describe statements or ideas, "相反" can mean "contradictory" indicating a situation where two things cannot both be true. For example:\n他们之间的说法是相反的。 - Their statements are contradictory.\n这些观点是相互相反的。 - These views are mutually contradictory.\n\nSo in summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "相反" can include "opposite", "contrary", "inverse", and "contradictory", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
    sentenceId: "相反",
    creator: "learnuidev@gmail.com",
