    summary:
      'The Chinese character "印象" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Impression\n\nThe most common translation of "印象" is "impression" when referring to a feeling, opinion, or impact left on someone. For example:\n我的第一印象很好。 - My first impression was very good.\n这个城市给人留下深刻的印象。 - This city leaves a deep impression on people.\n\n## 2. Print\n\n"印象" can also mean "print" in the context of printing or making copies. For example:\n这是一份彩色印象。 - This is a color print.\n请给我一份文件的印象。 - Please give me a copy of the document.\n\n## 3. Stamp\n\nIn certain contexts, "印象" can refer to a "stamp" used for printing or marking. For example:\n这枚邮票有一个美丽的印象。 - This stamp has a beautiful design.\n他的名字用印象盖在文件上。 - His name is stamped on the document.\n\n## 4. Influence\n\n"印象" can also mean "influence" when describing the impact or effect of something on a person or situation. For example:\n她的话对我产生了很大的印象。 - Her words had a great influence on me.\n这本书给了我很深的印象。 - This book left a deep impression on me.\n\nIn summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "印象" can include "impression", "print", "stamp", and "influence", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
