    summary:
      'The Persian word "سرزنش" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Rebuke\n\nThe most common translation of "سرزنش" is "rebuke", which means to express sharp disapproval or criticism of someone because of their actions. For example:\nوی او را به خاطر اشتباهش سرزنش کرد. - He rebuked him for his mistake.\n\n## 2. Reproach\n\n"سرزنش" can also mean "reproach", which is a mild rebuke or criticism. For example:\nپدرم هرگز مرا سرزنش نمی‌کند. - My father never reproaches me.\n\n## 3. Admonishment\n\nIn certain contexts, "سرزنش" can be translated as "admonishment", which is a firm warning or reprimand. For example:\nمعلم دانش‌آموزان را به دلیل تاخیر به مدرسه سرزنش می‌کند. - The teacher admonishes the students for being late to school.\n\n## 4. Blame\n\n"سرزنش" can also mean "blame", which is assigning responsibility for a fault or wrong. For example:\nاو به اشتباه سیاست‌های اقتصادی را بر او سرزنش می‌کند. - He wrongly blames him for the economic policies. \n\nIn summary, "سرزنش" can be translated as "rebuke", "reproach", "admonishment", or "blame", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
