    summary:
      'The Chinese character "耀" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Shine, Glitter\n\nThe most common translation of "耀" is "shine" or "glitter" when referring to something bright or dazzling. For example:\n星星在夜空中耀眼闪亮。 - The stars are shining brightly in the night sky.\n钻石闪耀着璀璨的光芒。 - The diamond is glittering with a brilliant light.\n\n## 2. Display, Show Off\n\n"耀" can also mean "display" or "show off" when describing someone\'s behavior or actions that draw attention or admiration. For example:\n他总是喜欢炫耀他的财富。 - He always likes to show off his wealth.\n她以自己的成就为她的家人们做事情感到自豪而不是炫耀。 - She takes pride in her achievements for her family rather than showing off.\n\n## 3. Honor, Glory\n\nIn certain contexts, "耀" can mean "honor" or "glory" when referring to fame or prestige. For example:\n那位运动员赢得了国家的荣耀。 - That athlete brought honor to the country.\n这座纪念碑是为了纪念那些为国家争光的英雄。 - This monument is in honor of the heroes who have brought glory to the country.\n\n## 4. Brilliant\n\nWhen used to describe a person, "耀" can mean "brilliant" or "outstanding". For example:\n他是一个聪明、有才华的年轻人，备受人们称道。 - He is a brilliant and talented young man who is highly praised.\n\nSo in summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "耀" can include "shine/glitter", "display/show off", "honor/glory", and "brilliant", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
