    summary:
      'The Romanian word "bătăi" can have multiple meanings in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Beatings\n\nThe most common translation of "bătăi" is "beatings" in English, referring to physical violence or hitting someone. For example:\nBăiatul a primit bătăi la școală. - The boy received beatings at school.\n\n## 2. Waves\n\nIn some contexts, "bătăi" can also mean "waves" in English, such as ocean waves or sound waves. For example:\nAuzi bătăile valurilor? - Do you hear the waves crashing?\n\n## 3. Pounding\n\nAnother translation of "bătăi" can be "pounding", referring to a rhythmic beating or pulsating. For example:\nAuzeați bătăile inimii sale puternice. - You could hear the pounding of his strong heart.\n\nIn summary, the Romanian word "bătăi" can be translated to English as "beatings", "waves", or "pounding", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
