    summary:
      'The Chinese character "忍" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Endure\n\nThe most common translation of "忍" is "endure" or "tolerate" when referring to bearing hardships or difficulties. For example:\n他能够忍受痛苦。 - He can endure pain.\n她无法忍受这种不公平的待遇。 - She cannot tolerate this unfair treatment.\n\n## 2. Forbearance\n\n"忍" can also mean "forbearance" or "patience" when describing the ability to control one\'s emotions or reactions. For example:\n要学会忍耐和宽容。 - Learn to have forbearance and tolerance.\n他有很强的忍耐力。 - He has a strong sense of forbearance.\n\n## 3. Refrain\n\nIn certain contexts, "忍" can mean "refrain" or "restrain" when advising against certain actions or behaviors. For example:\n忍住不发火。 - Hold back from getting angry.\n请忍住一下，不要说话。 - Please refrain from speaking for a moment.\n\n## 4. Tolerate\n\nAnother translation of "忍" can be "tolerate" when expressing the ability to endure something unpleasant or difficult. For example:\n她无法忍受这种行为。 - She cannot tolerate this behavior.\n你要有足够的忍耐和体谅。 - You need to have enough tolerance and understanding.\n\nIn summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "忍" can include "endure", "forbearance", "refrain", and "tolerate", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
