    summary:
      'The Chinese character "近" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Near, Close\n\nThe most common translation of "近" is "near" or "close" when referring to proximity in space or time. For example:\n我家离学校很近。 - My house is very close to the school.\n我们的会议就要开始了，请坐近一点。 - Our meeting is about to start, please sit closer.\n\n## 2. Recent, Latest\n\n"近" can also mean "recent" or "latest" when describing something that happened or was done recently. For example:\n最近的新闻 - The latest news\n她的近况怎么样？ - How is her recent situation?\n\n## 3. Similar, Almost\n\nIn certain contexts, "近" can signify "similar" or "almost" when comparing things or situations. For example:\n这个口味与我的偏好很近。- This flavor is very close to my preference.\n我们已经接近成功了。- We are getting close to success.\n\n## 4. Familiar, Intimate\n\nWhen used to describe relationships, "近" can mean "familiar" or "intimate". For example:\n他们是很熟近的朋友。- They are very close friends.\n\nOverall, the English translations of the Chinese character "近" can include "near/close", "recent/latest", "similar/almost", and "familiar/intimate", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
