      'The Chinese character "支" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Support\n\nThe most common translation of "支" is "support" when referring to providing assistance, help, or backing. For example:\n我会全力支持你的决定。 - I will fully support your decision.\n这个项目需要有政府的支持。 - This project needs government support.\n\n## 2. Branch\n\n"支" can also mean "branch" when describing a division or subdivision of an organization or structure. For example:\n这家公司在全国各地都有分支机构。 - This company has branches all over the country.\n银行的支行在这条街上。 - The bank branch is on this street.\n\n## 3. Stick\n\nIn certain contexts, "支" can mean "stick" when referring to a thin, elongated object. For example:\n这支笔用完了。 - This pen has run out.\n我需要一支新的牙刷。 - I need a new toothbrush.\n\n## 4. Counters for things like occurrences or units\n\nWhen used as a counter, "支" can be used to count things like occurrences or units. For example:\n一支牛奶 - one carton of milk\n两支笔 - two pens\n\nSo in summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "支" can include "support", "branch", "stick", and a counter for things like occurrences or units, depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
