      'The Chinese character "闪" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Flash, Sparkle\n\nThe most common translation of "闪" is "flash" or "sparkle" when referring to a sudden burst of light or a flickering movement. For example:\n闪电 - Lightning\n眼睛闪光 - Eyes sparkling\n\n## 2. Dodge, Evade\n\n"闪" can also mean "dodge" or "evade" when describing quick, nimble movements to avoid something. For example:\n闪避攻击 - Dodge an attack\n他躲在角落里闪开了 - He dodged away in the corner\n\n## 3. Quick, Rapid\n\nIn certain contexts, "闪" can convey the idea of being quick or rapid. For example:\n一闪而过 - Pass by in a flash\n行动迅速闪电 - Act like lightning\n\n## 4. Brief, Fleeting\n\nSometimes "闪" can imply something brief or fleeting, suggesting a momentary occurrence. For example:\n美丽的微笑闪现 - A beautiful smile flashed across\n瞬息即逝的甜蜜 - Fleeting sweetness\n\nTherefore, the English translations of the Chinese character "闪" can include "flash", "sparkle", "dodge", "evade", "quick", "rapid", "brief", and "fleeting", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
