    summary:
      'The Chinese character "分" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Divide, Separate\n\nOne common translation of "分" is "divide" or "separate" when referring to splitting things into parts. For example:\n请把这个苹果分成两半。 - Please divide this apple into two halves.\n我们需要把垃圾和可回收物分开。 - We need to separate the trash from the recyclables.\n\n## 2. Minute\n\n"分" can also mean "minute" when referring to time or a unit of measurement. For example:\n这种病毒可以在几分钟内传播。 - This virus can spread within minutes.\n这个小姐妹有五分之三的身高。 - This little sister is five minutes taller.\n\n## 3. Part, Portion\n\nIn certain contexts, "分" can mean "part" or "portion". For example:\n这是我的一份。 - This is my portion.\n每个人都应该承担自己的一份责任。 - Everyone should bear their own part of responsibility.\n\n## 4. Analysis\n\n"分" can also mean "analysis" when used in specific terms like 分析 (analyze) or 分解 (decompose). For example:\n这个问题需要仔细分析。 - This problem needs to be analyzed carefully.\n这种化学反应可以分解水。 - This chemical reaction can decompose water.\n\nIn summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "分" can include "divide/separate", "minute", "part/portion", and "analysis", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
