      'The Chinese character "得到" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Obtain, Get\n\nThe most common translation of "得到" is "obtain" or "get" when referring to acquiring something. For example:\n我得到了一份工作。 - I got a job.\n他得到了老板的夸奖。 - He received praises from the boss.\n\n## 2. Gain, Receive\n\n"得到" can also mean "gain" or "receive" when talking about obtaining something intangible. For example:\n他得到了成功。 - He achieved success.\n她得到了大家的支持。 - She received everyone\'s support.\n\n## 3. Realize\n\nIn certain contexts, "得到" can mean "realize" or "understand" when describing coming to a realization. For example:\n他终于得到了自己的错误。 - He finally realized his mistake.\n\n## 4. Attain, Reach\n\nWhen used in a more metaphorical sense, "得到" can mean "attain" or "reach" when talking about achieving a goal or reaching a certain status. For example:\n他得到了自己的目标。 - He achieved his goal.\n他得到了尊重。 - He attained respect.\n\nSo in summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "得到" can include "obtain/get", "gain/receive", "realize/understand", and "attain/reach", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
