      'The Chinese character "晚" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Late\n\nThe most common translation of "晚" is "late" when referring to time. For example:\n他今天晚上会很晚回家。 - He will come home very late tonight.\n这家店晚上十点就关门了。 - This shop closes at 10 o\'clock at night.\n\n## 2. Evening\n\n"晚" can also mean "evening" when specifying the time of day. For example:\n晚安 - Good evening\n晚餐 - Dinner/evening meal\n\n## 3. To decline, to worsen\n\nIn certain contexts, "晚" can mean "to decline" or "to worsen" when describing a situation or condition. For example:\n这种情况越来越晚。- This situation is getting worse and worse.\n今天的天气比昨天晚了。- Today\'s weather is worse than yesterday\'s.\n\nTherefore, the English translations of the Chinese character "晚" can include "late", "evening", and "to decline/to worsen", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
