      'The Chinese character "句" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Sentence\n\nThe most common translation of "句" is "sentence" when referring to a grammatical unit of words that expresses a complete thought. For example:\n这是一个简单的句子。- This is a simple sentence.\n这句话很有趣。- This sentence is very interesting.\n\n## 2. Clauses\n\n"句" can also refer to clauses within a sentence. For example:\n这句话包含两个子句。- This sentence contains two clauses.\n\n## 3. Phrase\n\nIn some contexts, "句" can also be translated as "phrase" when referring to a group of words that function as a unit in a sentence. For example:\n这是一个常用的短语句。- This is a commonly used phrase.\n\n## 4. Line (in poetry or music)\n\n"句" can also mean "line" when discussing poetry or music. For example:\n这首诗的每一句都很动人。- Every line of this poem is very moving.\n\nIn summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "句" can include "sentence", "clauses", "phrase", and "line", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
