    summary:
      'The Chinese character "义" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Righteousness, Justice\n\nThe most common translation of "义" is "righteousness" or "justice" when referring to moral principles or actions. For example:\n做义事 - Do righteous deeds\n追求正义 - Pursue justice\n\n## 2. Meaning, Significance\n\n"义" can also mean "meaning" or "significance" when describing the importance or interpretation of something. For example:\n有何深意？- What is the meaning/significance?\n这个符号有什么义？- What is the significance of this symbol?\n\n## 3. Benefit, Advantage\n\nIn certain contexts, "义" can also mean "benefit" or "advantage" when discussing a favorable outcome or gain. For example:\n这项计划有利于学生，对各方都有义。- This plan benefits students and is advantageous to all parties.\n\n## 4. Duty, Obligation\n\nWhen used in the sense of responsibility, "义" can mean "duty" or "obligation" towards someone or something. For example:\n尽义务 - Fulfill duties\n有保护弱者的义。- There is a duty to protect the weak.\n\nSo in summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "义" can include "righteousness/justice", "meaning/significance", "benefit/advantage", and "duty/obligation", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
