    summary:
      'The Arabic word "إنجاز" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Achievement\n\nThe most common translation of "إنجاز" is "achievement" when referring to successfully completing a task or reaching a goal. For example:\nهذا الإنجاز كان مذهلاً. - This achievement was amazing.\nأنا فخور بإنجازي. - I am proud of my achievement.\n\n## 2. Accomplishment\n\n"إنجاز" can also mean "accomplishment" when describing something that has been successfully completed. For example:\nأحسست بالسعادة بعد هذا الإنجاز. - I felt happy after this accomplishment.\nهذا إنجاز كبير للمشروع. - This is a great accomplishment for the project.\n\n## 3. Fulfillment\n\nIn certain contexts, "إنجاز" can imply a sense of fulfillment or satisfaction from completing a task or goal. For example:\nشعرت بالإنجاز بعد إتمام المهمة. - I felt a sense of fulfillment after completing the task.\nهذا العمل جلب لي الإنجاز الكبير. - This work brought me great fulfillment.\n\n## 4. Realization\n\nWhen used in some contexts, "إنجاز" can also mean "realization" in English, referring to the act of achieving or making something real. For example:\nهذا الإنجاز جعل حلمي حقيقة. - This realization made my dream a reality.\nإن الإنجازات تحتاج إلى جهد كبير. - Achievements require great effort.\n\nSo in summary, the English translations of the Arabic word "إنجاز" can include "achievement", "accomplishment", "fulfillment", and "realization", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
