      'The Chinese character "收" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Receive, Collect\n\nThe most common translation of "收" is "receive" or "collect" when referring to gathering or obtaining something. For example:\n收到包裹 - Receive a package\n收集资料 - Collect information\n\n## 2. Accept\n\n"收" can also mean "accept" when describing the action of taking something in. For example:\n收容 - Accept or take in\n收留 - Provide shelter or take in\n\n## 3. Income, Revenue\n\nIn certain contexts, "收" can mean "income" or "revenue" when referring to financial earnings. For example:\n收入 - Income\n收益 - Revenue\n\n## 4. Put Away, Put in Order\n\nWhen used in phrases like "收拾" or "整理", "收" can mean "put away" or "put in order". For example:\n收拾房间 - Tidy up the room\n整理文件 - Organize documents\n\nOverall, the English translations of the Chinese character "收" can include "receive/collect", "accept", "income/revenue", and "put away/put in order", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
