    summary:
      'The Persian character "پا" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Foot, Leg\n\nThe most common translation of "پا" is "foot" or "leg" when referring to a body part. For example:\nاو پاهای برهنه اش را در آب سرد فرو برد. - He dipped his bare feet into the cold water.\nبا یک پاستر روی پاهای خود خوابید. - She slept with a footstool under her feet.\n\n## 2. Step\n\n"پا" can also mean "step" when referring to a physical movement or progression. For example:\nبه آهستگی یک پا برداشت و به دیگری کشید. - She slowly took a step and then another one.\n\n## 3. Base, Foundation\n\nIn certain contexts, "پا" can mean "base" or "foundation" when referring to a supporting structure. For example:\nاین خانه یک پایه قوی دارد. - This house has a strong foundation.\nاین پل از چوب و اسمانها ساخته شده است. - This bridge is built of wood and has wooden supports.\n\n## 4. Get up\n\nWhen used as a verb, "پا" can mean "to get up" or "to rise". For example:\nاو از صندلی بلند شده و به ما خوش آمد گفت. - He got up from the chair and greeted us warmly.\nزورکی پا کن، دیر شده. - Get up quickly, it\'s late.\n\nSo in summary, the English translations of the Persian character "پا" can include "foot/leg", "step", "base/foundation", and "get up", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
