      'The Chinese character "其" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Its, Their, His, Her\n\n"其" can be translated as "its" when indicating possession or association. It can also mean "their", "his", or "her" depending on the context. For example:\n其颜色很漂亮。 - Its color is very beautiful.\n其它人已经离开了。 - The others have already left.\n\n## 2. That, Those\n\n"其" can also be translated as "that" or "those" when referring to something specific or previously mentioned. For example:\n其实情况并非如此。 - In fact, the situation is not like that.\n我看见了两个学生，其时在操场上玩。 - I saw two students, they were playing on the playground.\n\n## 3. His, Her\n\nIn some cases, "其" can also mean "his" or "her" when indicating possession. For example:\n其人其事 - His story, her story\n\nSo in summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "其" can include "its", "their", "his", "her", "that", and "those", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
