    summary:
      'The Chinese character "间" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Between, Among\n\nOne of the common translations of "间" is "between" or "among" when referring to the space or time separating things or events. For example:\n这两个城市之间有一条高速公路。- There is a highway between these two cities.\n我们之间有很深的友谊。- There is a deep friendship among us.\n\n## 2. Room, Space\n\n"间" can also mean "room" or "space" when describing a physical area or room. For example:\n客厅里有一间书房。- There is a study room in the living room.\n这个仓库的面积很大，有很多间。- This warehouse is large with many rooms/spaces.\n\n## 3. Gap, Interval\n\nIn certain contexts, "间" can refer to "gap" or "interval" between two points. For example:\n列车站在站之间有五分钟的停留时间。- The train stops for five minutes between stations.\n我们需要填补这段空白的间隙。- We need to fill in the gap in this blank space.\n\n## 4. Measure Word for Rooms\n\nAnother use of "间" is as a measure word for rooms or spaces. For example:\n这个房子有三间卧室。- This house has three bedrooms.\n我家有两间卫生间。- My home has two bathrooms.\n\nIn summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "间" can include "between/among", "room/space", "gap/interval", and as a measure word for rooms/spaces, depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
