    summary:
      'The Chinese character "同" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Same\n\nThe most common translation of "同" is "same" when referring to things or people that are identical or similar. For example:\n我们的爱好是一样的。 - Our hobbies are the same.\n他们穿着同样的衣服。 - They are wearing the same clothes.\n\n## 2. Together\n\n"同" can also mean "together" when describing actions or events done in unison or at the same time. For example:\n我们一起去吃饭吧。 - Let\'s go eat together.\n他们同时到达了机场。 - They arrived at the airport together.\n\n## 3. With\n\nIn certain contexts, "同" can mean "with" when indicating collaboration or partnership. For example:\n他们同事合作完成了这个项目。 - They worked together to complete this project.\n我们同学一起去旅行。 - We went on a trip with our classmates.\n\n## 4. Similar\n\n"同" can also mean "similar" when describing things that share common characteristics. For example:\n这两个词的意思很相同。 - The meanings of these two words are very similar.\n他的想法和我很同。 - His thoughts are very similar to mine.\n\nIn summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "同" can include "same", "together", "with", and "similar", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
