      'The Persian word "مهم" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Important\n\nThe most common translation of "مهم" is "important" when referring to something of significance or relevance. For example:\nاین موضوع بسیار مهم است. - This issue is very important.\nاین نکته برای ما بسیار مهم است. - This point is very important for us.\n\n## 2. Essential\n\n"مهم" can also mean "essential" when describing something that is crucial or necessary. For example:\nاین قانون برای حفظ امنیت ملی مهم است. - This law is essential for national security.\nاین یک اصل مهم در علم زندگی است. - This is an essential principle in the science of life.\n\n## 3. Significant\n\nIn certain contexts, "مهم" can be translated as "significant" when referring to something of importance or value. For example:\nاین یک پیشرفت مهم برای پروژه است. - This is a significant advancement for the project.\nفرهنگ ملی بخش مهمی از هویت ماست. - National culture is a significant part of our identity.\n\n## 4. Matter\n\nWhen used as a noun, "مهم" can also mean "matter" in English. For example:\nاین یک مهم معنوی برای او بود. - This was a spiritual matter for him.\nاین مهم مشترک بین همه ماست. - This is a common matter among all of us.\n\nIn summary, the English translations of the Persian word "مهم" can include "important", "essential", "significant", and "matter", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
