    summary:
      'The Chinese character "码" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Code\n\nOne common translation of "码" is "code" when referring to a system of signals, such as in computer programming or encryption. For example:\n这段代码有很多错误。 - This code has many errors.\n请将此信息转换为二进制码。 - Please convert this information to binary code.\n\n## 2. Yard\n\n"码" can also mean "yard" as a unit of measurement equal to three feet, often used in the context of length or distance. For example:\n这条布有多长？ - How long is this piece of fabric?\n这个篮球场有多少码长？ - How many yards long is this basketball court?\n\n## 3. Number\n\nIn certain contexts, "码" can also refer to a number or numeric value. For example:\n这个门牌号是多少码？ - What is the number of this doorplate?\n他获得了一个高分数。 - He received a high number.\n\n## 4. Mark\n\nWhen used as a verb, "码" can mean "to mark" or "to label" something. For example:\n请在文件上标记出问题所在。 - Please mark where the issue is on the document.\n我们需要把货物码好。 - We need to label the goods.\n\nIn summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "码" can include "code", "yard", "number", and "mark", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
