      'The Chinese character "题" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Topic, Subject\n\nOne common translation of "题" is "topic" or "subject" when referring to the theme or subject of something. For example:\n这个问题是这次演讲的主题。 - This question is the topic of the speech.\n这篇文章的主题很有意思。 - The subject of this article is very interesting.\n\n## 2. Title\n\n"题" can also mean "title" when used to refer to the heading or title of a piece of work. For example:\n书的题目是什么？ - What is the title of the book?\n这幅画的题字很有特色。 - The title of this painting is very distinctive.\n\n## 3. Mark, Label\n\nIn certain contexts, "题" can be translated as "mark" or "label" when indicating something is labeled or marked. For example:\n请在正确的答案上题一个星号。 - Please mark the correct answer with a star.\n这些文件需要题好号才能找得到。 - These documents need to be labeled properly in order to find them.\n\n## 4. Challenge, Question\n\nSometimes, "题" can also mean "challenge" or "question" when referring to a difficult problem or question. For example:\n这道数学题对我来说有些难题。 - This math problem is a challenging question for me.\n他喜欢解决各种各样的难题。 - He enjoys solving all kinds of difficult challenges.\n\nIn summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "题" can include "topic/subject", "title", "mark/label", and "challenge/question", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
