    summary:
      'The Chinese character "问" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Ask\n\nThe most common translation of "问" is "ask" when it is used as a verb to indicate the action of inquiring or questioning. For example:\n我想问一个问题。 - I want to ask a question.\n请问你的名字是什么？ - May I ask what your name is?\n\n## 2. Inquire, Interrogate\n\n"问" can also mean "inquire" or "interrogate" in a more formal or serious context, indicating a thorough questioning or investigation. For example:\n警察正在问他关于案件的细节。 - The police are questioning him about the details of the case.\n进行严格的审讯时通常会问很多问题。 - Many questions are usually asked during a rigorous interrogation.\n\n## 3. Consult\n\nIn certain situations, "问" can be translated as "consult" when it involves seeking advice or information from someone more knowledgeable. For example:\n我需要向医生问一下这个问题。 - I need to consult a doctor about this issue.\n明天我会去问老师关于作业的内容。 - Tomorrow I will consult the teacher about the homework.\n\n## 4. Street, Intersection\n\nIn some cases, "问" can also refer to "street" or "intersection" when used as a noun, indicating a location or place of questioning. For example:\n这条街道经过三个问路口。 - This street passes through three intersections.\n请问，这附近有商店吗？ - Excuse me, are there any shops around here?\n\nIn summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "问" can include "ask", "inquire/interrogate", "consult", or "street/intersection", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
