    summary:
      'The Chinese character "留" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Stay, Remain\n\nThe most common translation of "留" is "stay" or "remain" when referring to someone or something staying in a place. For example:\n他留在了家里。- He stayed at home.\n请留在这里等一下。- Please remain here for a moment.\n\n## 2. Keep, Preserve\n\n"留" can also mean "keep" or "preserve" when describing the act of maintaining something in its current state. For example:\n留住这份美好。- Keep/preserve this happiness.\n他留下了很多回忆。- He kept/preserved many memories.\n\n## 3. Leave, Retain\n\nIn certain contexts, "留" can mean "leave" or "retain" when referring to leaving something behind or retaining a particular quality. For example:\n留下来，我们一起走。- Stay/leave behind, let\'s go together.\n这款产品留有很多改进空间。- This product retains a lot of room for improvement.\n\n## 4. Memory, Record\n\nSometimes "留" can also refer to "memory" or "record," particularly in the context of preserving or leaving behind memories or records. For example:\n永远留在记忆中。- Forever stay in memory.\n留下重要的记录。- Leave behind important records.\n\nOverall, the English translations of the Chinese character "留" can include "stay/remain," "keep/preserve," "leave/retain," and "memory/record," depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
