    summary:
      'The Chinese character "援" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Support, Aid\n\nThe most common translation of "援" is "support" or "aid" when referring to assistance or help in a situation. For example:\n他们在地震后提供了援助。- They provided aid after the earthquake.\n国际社会纷纷伸出援助之手。- The international community extended a helping hand.\n\n## 2. Extract, Draw Out\n\n"援" can also mean "extract" or "draw out" when referring to the action of taking something out from a source. For example:\n他从口袋里援出了一封信。- He extracted a letter from his pocket.\n这种药可以援出身体内的毒素。- This medicine can draw out toxins from the body.\n\n## 3. Reinforce, Support\n\nIn certain contexts, "援" can mean "reinforce" or "support" in a military or strategic sense. For example:\n增援部队马上就会到达。- Reinforcement troops will arrive soon.\n他们需要援军支持以保护边境。- They need military support to protect the border.\n\n## 4. Cite, Quote\n\nAnother meaning of "援" is "cite" or "quote" when referring to referencing a source or providing evidence. For example:\n他援引了很多专家的观点来支持自己的论点。- He cited the opinions of many experts to support his argument.\n在论文中必须援引正确的资料。- Correct references must be quoted in the paper.\n\nIn summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "援" can include "support/aid", "extract/draw out", "reinforce/support", and "cite/quote", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
