    summary:
      'The Chinese character "由" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. By, From\n\nThe most common translation of "由" is "by" or "from" when indicating the starting point or cause. For example:\n由北京到上海需要坐火车。 - Traveling from Beijing to Shanghai requires taking the train.\n这个问题由他引起。 - This problem was caused by him.\n\n## 2. Through, Via\n\n"由" can also mean "through" or "via" when indicating a method or route. For example:\n我们可以通过邮件沟通。 - We can communicate via email.\n这个计划由多个阶段组成。 - This plan consists of multiple stages.\n\n## 3. Because of, Due to\n\nIn certain contexts, "由" can be translated as "because of" or "due to" when expressing a reason or cause. For example:\n由于天气原因，比赛被取消了。 - The match was canceled due to the weather.\n他的成功由他的努力而来。 - His success comes from his hard work.\n\n## 4. In charge\n\nWhen used as a noun, "由" can mean "in charge" or "by" when referring to someone who is responsible or in control. For example:\n这个项目由他负责。 - He is in charge of this project.\n这场比赛由裁判掌控。 - The referee is in charge of this game.\n\nOverall, the English translations of the Chinese character "由" can include "by/from", "through/via", "because of/due to", and "in charge", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
