      'The Chinese character "连同" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Together with\n\nThe most common translation of "连同" is "together with" when indicating things being joined or included. For example:\n他连同家人一起前往。 - He went together with his family.\n连同这封信一起寄出。 - Send it out together with this letter.\n\n## 2. Along with\n\n"连同" can also be translated as "along with" in situations where something is accompanying or included with another thing. For example:\n她连同礼物一起来了。 - She came along with a gift.\n这本书连同其他资料都很有用。 - This book, along with other materials, is very useful.\n\n## 3. Including\n\nIn certain contexts, "连同" can mean "including" when emphasizing the inclusion of something. For example:\n这次活动连同午餐在内都是免费的。 - This event, including lunch, is free of charge.\n这份报告连同所有附件一起提交。 - Submit this report including all attachments.\n\n## 4. Together\n\nWhen used in a more general sense, "连同" can simply mean "together" or "combined". For example:\n他们连同努力才取得了成功。 - They achieved success through combined efforts.\n我们应该连同努力，共同完成任务。 - We should work together to complete the task.\n\nIn summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "连同" can include "together with", "along with", "including", and "together", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
