    summary:
      'The Chinese character "间" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Between, Among\n\nThe most common translation of "间" is "between" or "among" when indicating a relationship or spatial separation. For example:\n这两栋建筑之间有一个花园。 - There is a garden between these two buildings.\n我们之间有些误会。 - There are some misunderstandings among us.\n\n## 2. Room, Space\n\n"间" can also mean "room" or "space" when referring to a physical area or enclosure. For example:\n这个房间很宽敞明亮。 - This room is spacious and bright.\n书架之间留有一些空间。 - There is some space left between the bookshelves.\n\n## 3. Interval\n\nIn certain contexts, "间" can represent an "interval" or "gap" between two things or points in time. For example:\n课间休息 - Recess (literally: class interval break)\n两次会议之间有一个小时的间隔。 - There is an hour interval between the two meetings.\n\n## 4. Measure Word\n\n"间" can also function as a measure word for houses, buildings, rooms, etc., similar to "个" in English. For example:\n两间卧室 - Two bedrooms\n一间饭馆 - A restaurant\n\nOverall, the English translations of the Chinese character "间" can include "between", "among", "room", "space", "interval", and as a measure word, depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
