    summary:
      'The Chinese character "适" can have several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Suitable, Appropriate\n\nThe most common translation of "适" is "suitable" or "appropriate" when referring to something that fits well or is suitable for a certain purpose. For example:\n这件衣服很适合你。 - This clothing suits you well.\n这个工作很适合我的能力。 - This job is very suitable for my abilities.\n\n## 2. To Adapt\n\n"适" can also mean "to adapt" when describing the process of adjusting or changing to fit a new situation. For example:\n他很快适应了新的环境。 - He quickly adapted to the new environment.\n这种技术需要适时更新。 - This technology needs to be updated in a timely manner.\n\n## 3. Proper, Fit\n\nIn certain contexts, "适" can mean "proper" or "fit" when referring to something that is correct or appropriate. For example:\n这是一个适当的解决方案。 - This is a proper solution.\n每天做一些适量的运动对健康有好处。 - Doing a proper amount of exercise every day is beneficial for health.\n\n## 4. Experience\n\nWhen used in a different context, "适" can also mean "experience" or "undergo". For example:\n这是我第一次适应这种情况。 - This is my first time experiencing this situation.\n他经历了很多适应生活的挑战。 - He has undergone many challenges in adapting to life.\n\nSo in summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "适" can include "suitable/appropriate", "to adapt", "proper/fit", and "experience", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
