    summary:
      'The Chinese character "疑" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Doubt\n\nThe most common translation of "疑" is "doubt" when referring to a feeling of uncertainty or lack of conviction. For example:\n对他的话我始终有些疑惑。 - I always have some doubts about what he says.\n他对这个计划表示了怀疑。 - He expressed doubts about this plan.\n\n## 2. Suspect\n\n"疑" can also mean "suspect" when referring to being doubtful about someone or something. For example:\n他被警方怀疑有犯罪行为。 - He is suspected by the police of criminal activity.\n我对这次事故的起因感到怀疑。 - I have suspicions about the cause of this accident.\n\n## 3. Skeptical\n\nIn certain contexts, "疑" can convey the idea of being "skeptical" or showing doubt towards something. For example:\n他对这个理论持怀疑态度。 - He is skeptical of this theory.\n我对这个项目的成功前景感到怀疑。 - I am skeptical about the success prospects of this project.\n\n## 4. Question\n\nWhen used as a verb, "疑" can mean "to question" or "to doubt the truth or validity of something". For example:\n他开始质疑上级的决定。 - He started to question the decisions made by his superiors.\n她疑惑地看着他，不知道该相信还是怀疑。 - She looked at him with doubt, unsure whether to believe or doubt.\n\nSo in summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "疑" can include "doubt", "suspect", "skeptical", and "question", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
