    summary:
      'The Korean character "검" has several meanings and translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Sword\n\nOne of the primary translations of "검" is "sword". It refers to a weapon with a long, sharp blade typically used for cutting or thrusting. For example:\n그의 손에는 검이 있었다. - He had a sword in his hand.\n\n## 2. Check\n\n"검" can also mean "check" in certain contexts, such as examining or inspecting something for accuracy, errors, or quality. For example:\n문서를 검토해 주세요. - Please check/review the document.\n\n## 3. Search\n\nIn another context, "검" can also be translated as "search", often used to refer to looking for something or investigating. For example:\n정보를 검색하다. - To search for information.\n\n## 4. Dark\n\nAdditionally, "검" can represent the color "black" or the concept of darkness. For example:\n이 방은 검은 색으로 칠해져 있다. - This room is painted in black.\n\nTherefore, depending on the specific context in which it is used, the English translations of the Korean character "검" can include "sword", "check", "search", and "dark".',
