    summary:
      'The Chinese character "固" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Firm, Solid\n\nOne of the meanings of "固" is "firm" or "solid", indicating something that is stable and unyielding. For example:\n这座城墙很固。 - This city wall is very solid.\n她的态度非常固执。 - Her attitude is very firm.\n\n## 2. Fixed, Set\n\n"固" can also mean "fixed" or "set", emphasizing the idea of being unchanging or immovable. For example:\n价格已经固定了。 - The price has been fixed.\n他们已经固定了下周的会议日期。 - They have set the date for the meeting next week.\n\n## 3. Guarantee\n\nIn certain contexts, "固" can also mean "guarantee" or "guaranteed". For example:\n我们会给您一个固定的价格。 - We will give you a guaranteed price.\n这家公司提供品质固定的产品。 - This company provides products with guaranteed quality.\n\n## 4. Secure\n\nWhen used in a more abstract sense, "固" can convey the idea of being secure or stable. For example:\n政府正在努力确保国家的固定。 - The government is working hard to ensure the stability of the country.\n\nSo in summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "固" can include "firm/solid", "fixed/set", "guarantee", and "secure", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
