      'The Japanese character "察" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Observe, Investigate\n\nThe most common translation of "察" is "observe" or "investigate" when referring to perceiving or examining carefully. For example:\n彼は状況をよく察する。- He observes the situation well.\n警察は事件を徹底的に察する。- The police thoroughly investigate the case.\n\n## 2. Guess, Sense\n\n"察" can also mean "guess" or "sense" when describing the act of making an inference or intuitively perceiving something. For example:\n彼女は私の気持ちを敏感に察した。- She sensed my feelings keenly.\n状況から事情を察する。- To guess the circumstances from the situation.\n\n## 3. Check, Inspect\n\nIn certain contexts, "察" can mean "check" or "inspect" when referring to examining or verifying something carefully. For example:\n証拠を察する。- To check the evidence.\n材料を熟練に察す。- To inspect materials carefully.\n\n## 4. Perceive, Understand\n\nWhen used as a verb, "察" can also mean "perceive" or "understand" the nature or meaning of something. For example:\n彼の言動から意図を察する。- To understand the intention from his words and actions.\n状況から事態を察する。- To perceive the situation.\n\nSo in summary, the English translations of the Japanese character "察" can include "observe/investigate", "guess/sense", "check/inspect", and "perceive/understand", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
