    summary:
      'The Chinese character "不" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Not\n\nThe most common translation of "不" is "not" when used to negate a statement or action. For example:\n我不知道。 - I don\'t know.\n他不喜欢吃辣的食物。 - He doesn\'t like spicy food.\n\n## 2. No\n\n"不" can also mean "no" when used to reject or refuse something. For example:\n我不要。 - No, I don\'t want it.\n他不同意这个决定。 - He disagrees with this decision.\n\n## 3. To be without, lacking\n\nIn certain contexts, "不" can convey the meaning of being without or lacking something. For example:\n穷人不但没有钱，还没有房子。 - The poor not only have no money, but also have no houses.\n他不耐烦。 - He is impatient.\n\n## 4. Negative prefix\n\n"不" is commonly used as a negative prefix for verbs, adjectives, and nouns to indicate the opposite or absence of the following word\'s meaning. For example:\n不可能 - Impossible\n不幸福 - Unhappy\n\nIn summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "不" include "not", "no", "to be without/lacking", and as a negative prefix, depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
