    summary:
      'The Chinese character "格" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Grid, Pattern\n\nOne of the meanings of "格" is "grid" or "pattern" when referring to a structured arrangement or design. For example:\n这幅画的格子很有特点。 - The grid pattern on this painting is very distinctive.\n这个地区的道路呈现网格状。 - The roads in this area form a grid pattern.\n\n## 2. Standard, Criterion\n\n"格" can also mean "standard" or "criterion" when discussing requirements or expectations. For example:\n他符合我们公司的招聘格。 - He meets the hiring standard of our company.\n这个产品不符合质量格。 - This product does not meet the quality standard.\n\n## 3. Compartment\n\nIn certain contexts, "格" can refer to a "compartment" or "partition" that divides a space. For example:\n这个书架有很多格，可以放很多书。 - This bookshelf has many compartments, can hold a lot of books.\n这间房间通过格子墙分隔成两部分。 - This room is divided into two parts by a partition wall.\n\n## 4. Genre\n\nWhen used in the context of literature or art, "格" can also be translated as "genre" or "style". For example:\n这本书是科幻格的。 - This book is in the genre of science fiction.\n他擅长绘画不同的格。 - He is skilled in painting different styles.\n\nSo, in summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "格" can include "grid/pattern", "standard/criterion", "compartment", and "genre/style", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
