      'The Chinese character "年" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Year\n\nThe most common translation of "年" is "year" when referring to a period of time. For example:\n去年 - last year\n明年 - next year\n\n## 2. Age\n\n"年" can also mean "age" when describing how old someone is. For example:\n他今年二十岁了。 - He is twenty years old this year.\n他年纪大了。 - He is getting old.\n\n## 3. Annual\n\nIn certain contexts, "年" can be translated as "annual" when referring to something that occurs yearly or is related to a year. For example:\n年度报告 - annual report\n年会 - annual meeting\n\n## 4. Years of Experience\n\nWhen used in the context of experience or seniority, "年" can indicate "years of experience" or "years of service". For example:\n他有丰富的工作经验，有十年以上的工作年限。 - He has rich work experience and over ten years of work experience.\n他是公司的老员工，已经工作了很多年。 - He is a senior employee of the company and has been working for many years.\n\nSo in summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "年" can include "year", "age", "annual", and "years of experience", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
