    summary:
      'The Chinese character "不了" does not have a direct translation into English because it is not a standalone character but a combination of two characters "不" and "了".\n\n## 1. "不" - Not, No\n\nThe character "不" translates to "not" or "no" in English. It is used to negate a verb or adjective. For example:\n我不想去。 - I don\'t want to go.\n这个问题我不知道。 - I don\'t know the answer to this question.\n\n## 2. "了" - Indicates completion or change\n\nThe character "了" has multiple meanings, one of which is indicating the completion of an action or a change in a situation. For example:\n我吃了饭。 - I have eaten.\n他生病了。 - He got sick.\n\nWhen combined, "不了" does not have a specific meaning on its own but can be part of a sentence where "不" and "了" modify the verb or describe a situation.',
