    summary:
      'The Chinese character "到" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. To Arrive\n\nThe most common translation of "到" is "to arrive" when indicating reaching a destination. For example:\n我们几点到家？ - What time will we arrive home?\n火车几点到站？ - What time will the train arrive at the station?\n\n## 2. To Reach\n\n"到" can also mean "to reach" when describing the action of getting to a certain point. For example:\n他的事业达到了新的高度。 - His career has reached new heights.\n水平到了可以比赛的程度。 - The level has reached a point where we can compete.\n\n## 3. Up To\n\nIn certain contexts, "到" can be translated as "up to" when indicating a specific limit or extent. For example:\n我等你等到几点？ - How late should I wait for you?\n这个商店营业时间到晚上十点。 - This shop is open until 10 p.m.\n\n## 4. To\n\nWhen used as a preposition, "到" can simply mean "to" when indicating a direction or destination. For example:\n我们走到公园。 - We walk to the park.\n飞机飞到了美国。 - The plane flew to America.\n\nIn summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "到" can include "to arrive", "to reach", "up to", and "to", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
