    summary:
      'The Chinese character "用" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Use\n\nThe most common translation of "用" is "use" when referring to utilizing something for a specific purpose. For example:\n请用筷子吃饭。 - Please use chopsticks to eat.\n这种工具很容易使用。 - This tool is very easy to use.\n\n## 2. With\n\n"用" can also mean "with" when describing the instrument or means by which something is done. For example:\n她用手机给我发了短信。 - She sent me a text message with her phone.\n他用泥土建造了一个房子。 - He built a house with mud.\n\n## 3. Employ\n\nIn certain contexts, "用" can be translated as "employ" when referring to using something for a specific purpose or task. For example:\n我们需要用更多的资源来完成这项工作。 - We need to employ more resources to complete this task.\n用心思考。 - Employ your mind/think carefully.\n\n## 4. Need\n\nSometimes "用" can also express the idea of "need" when indicating a requirement or necessity. For example:\n这种情况下需要用更多的时间来解决。 - More time is needed to solve the situation.\n这个工作需要用心完成。 - This task needs to be completed with care.\n\nIn summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "用" can include "use", "with", "employ", and "need", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
