      'The Chinese character "忘" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Forget\n\nThe most common translation of "忘" is "forget" when referring to memory or forgetting something. For example:\n我忘了带钱包。- I forgot to bring my wallet.\n不要忘记明天的会议。- Don\'t forget about the meeting tomorrow.\n\n## 2. Neglect\n\n"忘" can also mean "neglect" when describing the act of neglecting or ignoring something. For example:\n不能忘了健康。- Don\'t neglect your health.\n他忙于工作，经常忘了休息。- He is busy with work and often neglects to rest.\n\n## 3. Abandon\n\nIn certain contexts, "忘" can mean "abandon" when referring to leaving something behind or forsaking. For example:\n不要忘了你的信仰。- Don\'t abandon your faith.\n他忘掉了过去的失败，重新开始了。- He abandoned his past failures and started anew.\n\n## 4. Oblivion\n\nAnother translation for "忘" can be "oblivion" when describing a state of forgetfulness or oblivion. For example:\n有些事情一旦忘却，就像从记忆中消失了一样。- Some things, once forgotten, disappear into oblivion in memory.\n他被时间的洪流冲走，最终陷入永恒的忘却之中。- He was washed away by the river of time, ultimately sinking into eternal oblivion.\n\nOverall, in English, "忘" can be translated as "forget", "neglect", "abandon", or "oblivion", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
