    summary:
      'The Chinese character "当" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Serve as, Act as\n\nOne of the common translations of "当" is "serve as" or "act as", indicating the role or function of something or someone. For example:\n我会当你的翻译。 - I will serve as your translator.\n他当了十年的老师。 - He has been acting as a teacher for ten years.\n\n## 2. When, While\n\n"Dang" can also mean "when" or "while" in certain contexts, indicating a specific time or condition. For example:\n当我看到她时，她正在哭。 - When I saw her, she was crying.\n当你学习时，我会做晚饭。 - While you study, I will make dinner.\n\n## 3. Pass, Succeed\n\nIn some situations, "当" can mean "pass" or "succeed" when referring to an examination, test, or challenge. For example:\n他当上了总经理。 - He succeeded in becoming the general manager.\n她考试当了。 - She passed the exam.\n\n## 4. Accept, Bear\n\nWhen used in certain phrases or expressions, "当" can mean "accept" or "bear" a responsibility or role. For example:\n当父母的责任 - Accepting the responsibility of being a parent\n当局者迷 - Those involved are often confused\n\nIn summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "当" can include "serve as/act as", "when/while", "pass/succeed", and "accept/bear", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
