    summary:
      'The Chinese character "溜" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Slip, Slide\n\nThe most common translation of "溜" is "slip" or "slide" when referring to movement. For example:\n他溜进了房间。 - He slipped into the room.\n小狗在溜滑梯上玩耍。 - The puppy is playing on the slide.\n\n## 2. Sneak, Slink\n\n"溜" can also mean "sneak" or "slink" when describing moving quietly or in a secretive manner. For example:\n他溜出了家门。 - He snuck out of the house.\n她溜进了房间，想给他一个惊喜。 - She sneaked into the room to surprise him.\n\n## 3. Skilled, Proficient\n\nIn certain contexts, "溜" can mean "skilled" or "proficient" when describing someone\'s abilities. For example:\n他在厨艺方面很溜。 - He is very skilled in cooking.\n她溜着笔写了一封漂亮的信。 - She proficiently wrote a beautiful letter.\n\n## 4. Water Pool\n\nSometimes, "溜" can refer to a pool of water or a place where water collects. For example:\n雨后地上形成了一个溜。 - A pool of water formed on the ground after the rain.\n这个地方容易积水成溜。 - This place easily collects water into pools.\n\nIn summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "溜" can include "slip/slide", "sneak/slink", "skilled/proficient", and "water pool", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
