      'The Persian word "خورد" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Eat\n\nThe most common translation of "خورد" is "eat" when referring to consuming food. For example:\nاو غذا می‌خورد. - He is eating food.\nاین صبح چه چیزی خوردی؟ - What did you eat this morning?\n\n## 2. Drink\n\n"خورد" can also mean "drink" when referring to consuming liquids. For example:\nاو آب می‌خورد. - He is drinking water.\nدرمانی که باید بخورم - The medicine I have to drink\n\n## 3. Bite\n\nIn certain contexts, "خورد" can mean "bite" when referring to taking a bite of something. For example:\nاو یک تکه از سیب را خورد. - He took a bite of the apple.\nسگ من دامنم را گاز خورد - My dog bit my skirt\n\n## 4. Wear away\n\nWhen used in a metaphorical sense, "خورد" can mean "wear away" or "erode". For example:\nاین باران سنگ‌ها را می‌خورد. - This rain is eroding the stones.\nاین بارون ماهیچه‌ها را می‌خورد - This rain erodes the muscles\n\nIn summary, the English translations of the Persian word "خورد" can include "eat", "drink", "bite", and "wear away", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
