    summary:
      'The Chinese character "图" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Picture, Image\n\nThe most common translation of "图" is "picture" or "image" when referring to visual representations. For example:\n这幅图很美丽。 - This picture is very beautiful.\n她在网上分享了一张猫咪的图。 - She shared an image of a cat online.\n\n## 2. Chart, Diagram\n\n"图" can also mean "chart" or "diagram" when referring to visual aids that display information. For example:\n这份报告中有很多图表。 - There are many charts in this report.\n这张地图显示了城市的道路网络。 - This map shows the city\'s road network.\n\n## 3. Plan, Scheme\n\nIn certain contexts, "图" can mean "plan" or "scheme" when referring to a detailed proposal or strategy. For example:\n他制定了一个学习计划的图。 - He made a plan for his study schedule.\n政府出台了一项扶贫图。 - The government introduced a poverty alleviation plan.\n\n## 4. To Design, To Draw\n\nWhen used as a verb, "图" can mean "to design" or "to draw". For example:\n她喜欢图案设计。 - She enjoys designing patterns.\n他会用软件图出建筑设计。 - He can draw architectural designs using software.\n\nSo in summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "图" can include "picture/image", "chart/diagram", "plan/scheme", and "to design/to draw", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
