      'The Chinese character "牧" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Herd\n\nThe most common translation of "牧" is "herd," referring to the act of tending or managing a group of animals. For example:\n牧羊人 - Shepherd\n牧场 - Pasture\n\n## 2. Grazing\n\n"牧" can also mean "grazing" or "pastoral" when describing land used for the feeding of livestock. For example:\n牧草 - Pasture grass\n牧业 - Animal husbandry\n\n## 3. Shepherd, Herdsman\n\nIn certain contexts, "牧" can refer to a "shepherd" or "herdsman," someone who cares for and manages livestock. For example:\n牧师 - Pastor (literally "shepherd")\n放牧 - Grazing livestock\n\nTherefore, the English translations of the Chinese character "牧" can include "herd," "grazing/pastoral," and "shepherd/herdsman," depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
