      'The Urdu word چھوڑنا has different translations in English depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Leave\n\nThe most common translation of "چھوڑنا" is "leave" when referring to abandoning or departing from a place or situation. For example:\nوہ شہر چھوڑ چکا ہے۔ - He has left the city.\nمیں نے اس کو چھوڑ دیا۔ - I have left him.\n\n## 2. Drop\n\n"چھوڑنا" can also mean "drop" when referring to letting something fall or abandoning it. For example:\nوہ چابی چھوڑ گئی۔ - She dropped the key.\nاس مسئلے کو چھوڑ دیں۔ - Let\'s drop this issue.\n\n## 3. Quit\n\nIn certain contexts, "چھوڑنا" can mean "quit" when referring to giving up or relinquishing something. For example:\nوہ کام چھوڑ دیا ہے۔ - He has quit the job.\nچھوڑ دو یہ ناچیزیں۔ - Quit these trivial matters.\n\n## 4. Release\n\nWhen used in a different context, "چھوڑنا" can mean "release" when setting something free or letting go. For example:\nوہ قیدی چھوڑ گیا۔ - The prisoner was released.\nہاتھ چھوڑ دو! - Let go of my hand!\n\nIn summary, the English translations of the Urdu word "چھوڑنا" can include "leave", "drop", "quit", and "release", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
