      'The Hindi term "गाना" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Song\n\nThe most common translation of "गाना" is "song" when referring to a musical composition with vocals. For example:\nमैंने एक नया गाना सुना। - I heard a new song.\nवह गाना बहुत पसंद करता है। - He loves that song.\n\n## 2. Sing\n\n"गाना" can also mean "to sing" when used as a verb to perform vocal music. For example:\nवह बहुत अच्छे तरीके से गाता है। - He sings very well.\nमैंने कभी सोनू निगम का गाना सुना है। - I have heard Sonu Nigam sing before.\n\n## 3. Chant\n\nIn certain contexts, "गाना" can refer to chanting or reciting verses or mantras. For example:\nउन्होंने आध्यात्मिक गाना किया। - They chanted spiritual verses.\nगाना करने से मन शांत हो जाता है। - Chanting brings peace to the mind.\n\n## 4. Perform\n\nWhen used in a broader sense, "गाना" can mean "to perform" or "to recite" any form of vocal expression. For example:\nवे गाना उस नाटक में किया। - They performed in that play.\nकृष्ण भक्ति का गाना करते हुए। - Reciting songs of devotion to Krishna.\n\nIn summary, the English translations of the Hindi term "गाना" can include "song", "sing", "chant", and "perform", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
