    summary:
      'The Chinese character "像" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Resemble, Like\n\nThe most common translation of "像" is "resemble" or "like" when describing similarities between things or people. For example:\n他像他爸爸。 - He resembles his father.\n这个画像像我妈妈。 - This portrait looks like my mother.\n\n## 2. Image, Picture\n\n"像" can also mean "image" or "picture" when referring to visual representations. For example:\n这幅画是她的肖像。 - This painting is her portrait.\n这张照片是我的全家福像。 - This photo is a picture of my whole family.\n\n## 3. Worship, Idolize\n\nIn certain contexts, "像" can mean "worship" or "idolize" when describing admiration or devotion towards someone or something. For example:\n她像个明星一样受欢迎。 - She is worshipped like a star.\n他将领袖像神一样崇拜。 - He worships the leader like a god.\n\n## 4. Such as\n\nWhen used as a conjunction, "像" can also mean "such as" to introduce examples or comparisons. For example:\n一些水果像苹果、香蕉等都很健康。 - Fruits such as apples, bananas, etc., are very healthy.\n\nSo in summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "像" can include "resemble/like", "image/picture", "worship/idolize", and "such as", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
