    summary:
      'The Chinese character "常" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Often, Commonly\n\nOne of the main translations of "常" is "often" or "commonly", referring to frequency or regularity. For example:\n他常常去图书馆。- He often goes to the library.\n这是我们常见的问题。- This is a common problem for us.\n\n## 2. Normal, Regular\n\n"常" can also mean "normal" or "regular" when describing something consistent or habitual. For example:\n她的工作日常。- Her work is regular.\n这家餐厅的服务态度很常。- The service attitude of this restaurant is normal.\n\n## 3. Constant, Always\n\nIn certain contexts, "常" can convey the idea of "constant" or "always". For example:\n他对学习很认真，常获奖学金。- He is very serious about studying and always wins scholarships.\n\n## 4. Chief, Principal\n\nSometimes, "常" can mean "chief" or "principal" when referring to a leader or key figure. For example:\n公司的常务董事- The company\'s chief executive officer.\n\nIn summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "常" can include "often", "commonly", "normal", "regular", "constant", "always", and "chief/principal", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
