      'The Chinese character "付" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Pay\n\nThe most common translation of "付" is "pay" when referring to making a payment. For example:\n我要付款。 - I want to pay.\n请把钱付给他。 - Please pay him the money.\n\n## 2. Hand over, Submit\n\n"付" can also mean "hand over" or "submit" when describing the action of giving something to someone or submitting a document. For example:\n他付了护照。 - He handed over the passport.\n请在截止日期前付交作业。 - Please submit the assignment before the deadline.\n\n## 3. According to\n\nIn certain contexts, "付" can also mean "according to" when referring to something being done in accordance with a particular standard or requirement. For example:\n付公司规定执行。 - According to company regulations.\n\n## 4. Cover\n\nWhen used as a verb, "付" can mean "to cover" or "to take care of expenses". For example:\n这笔费用由公司付。 - This expense is covered by the company.\n这家餐馆付了我的饭钱。 - This restaurant paid for my meal.\n\nSo in summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "付" can include "pay", "hand over/submit", "according to", and "cover", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
