      'The Chinese character "随" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Follow\n\nThe most common translation of "随" is "follow" when referring to following someone or something. For example:\n请随我来。 - Please follow me.\n他总是随着音乐跳舞。 - He always dances along with the music.\n\n## 2. Along with, In accordance with\n\n"随" can also mean "along with" or "in accordance with" when describing actions or events that happen together or in relation to something else. For example:\n随时间的推移，他越来越聪明。 - Along with the passage of time, he became smarter and smarter.\n他们制定了一个随时准备的计划。 - They made a plan that they can implement at any time.\n\n## 3. Random, Casual\n\nIn certain contexts, "随" can mean "random" or "casual" when describing something without a specific order or plan. For example:\n今天吃什么？随便吧。 - What do you want to eat today? Anything is fine/casual.\n\n## 4. Accompany\n\nWhen used as a verb, "随" can mean "to accompany" or "to be with someone or something". For example:\n他的狗总是随着他。 - His dog always accompanies him.\n车站附近有警察随伴。 - Police officers are stationed near the station.\n\nSo in summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "随" can include "follow", "along with/in accordance with", "random/casual", and "accompany", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
