      'The Chinese character "一直" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Always, continuously\n\nThe most common translation of "一直" is "always" or "continuously" when describing actions or states that have been ongoing without interruption. For example:\n他一直在学习。 - He has been studying continuously.\n我一直喜欢音乐。 - I have always liked music.\n\n## 2. Straight, direct\n\n"一直" can also mean "straight" or "direct" when describing a continuous line or path without turning or deviating. For example:\n一直走就到了。 - Just keep going straight and you will arrive.\n她一直盯着他看。 - She stared at him directly.\n\n## 3. All along\n\nIn certain contexts, "一直" can mean "all along" when expressing a continuous state or action that has been true or ongoing throughout a period of time. For example:\n他一直知道这个秘密。 - He has known this secret all along.\n她一直在等你。 - She has been waiting for you all along.\n\nIn summary, the English translations of the Chinese characters "一直" can include "always/continuously", "straight/direct", and "all along", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
