    summary:
      'The Chinese character "面" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Noodle, Dough\n\nOne common translation of "面" is "noodle" or "dough" when referring to food made from flour paste. For example:\n这家餐馆的手工面很好吃。 - The handmade noodles at this restaurant are very tasty.\n奶奶在桌子上擀面。- Grandma is rolling out dough on the table.\n\n## 2. Surface, Face\n\n"面" can also mean "surface" or "face" when describing the outer part of something. For example:\n这个多面体有很多边。- This polyhedron has many faces.\n他的脸上露出了微笑的面孔。- A smiling face appeared on his face.\n\n## 3. Aspect, Side\n\nIn certain contexts, "面" can represent different aspects or sides of a situation. For example:\n从环境保护的面来看 - From the perspective of environmental protection\n我们需要考虑这个问题的各个面。- We need to consider all aspects of this issue.\n\n## 4. Flour\n\n"面" can also refer to "flour" when discussing ingredients or cooking. For example:\n这种面粉适合做面包。- This flour is suitable for making bread.\n\nOverall, the English translations of the Chinese character "面" can include "noodle/dough", "surface/face", "aspect/side", and "flour", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
