    summary:
      'The Chinese character "简" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Simple\n\nThe most common translation of "简" is "simple" when referring to something that is easy, uncomplicated, or not complex. For example:\n这个问题很简单。 - This problem is very simple.\n她的服装风格很简洁。 - Her clothing style is very simple.\n\n## 2. Brief, Concise\n\n"简" can also mean "brief" or "concise" when describing something that is short and to the point. For example:\n请简单介绍一下你的工作经历。 - Please briefly introduce your work experience.\n这篇文章写得很简洁。 - This article is written very concisely.\n\n## 3. Simplified\n\nIn certain contexts, "简" can refer to something that has been simplified or made easier. For example:\n这是简化版的说明书。 - This is a simplified version of the manual.\n这个软件提供了简易操作的界面。 - This software provides a simplified user interface.\n\n## 4. Easy\n\nWhen used as an adjective, "简" can also mean "easy" or "not difficult". For example:\n这道数学题很简单。 - This math problem is very easy.\n学会这个软件很简易。 - Learning this software is very easy.\n\nSo in summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "简" can include "simple", "brief/concise", "simplified", and "easy", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
