    summary:
      'The Chinese character "飞" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n1. **Fly**\n\nThe most common translation of "飞" is "fly" when referring to the action of flying. For example:\n   - 鸟在天空中飞。 - The bird is flying in the sky.\n   - 飞机正在飞向国际空港。 - The airplane is flying towards the international airport.\n\n2. **Flee**\n\n"飞" can also mean "flee" or "escape" when describing actions related to quickly leaving a place. For example:\n   - 他们听到枪声后立刻飞奔逃离。 - They immediately fled when they heard gunshots.\n   - 在骚乱开始时，居民们纷纷飞向安全的地方。 - When the riot started, residents fled to safe places.\n\n3. **Swift**\n\nIn certain contexts, "飞" can mean "swift" or "rapid" when describing fast movements or actions. For example:\n   - 他的拳击速度快得像闪电一样。 - His boxing speed is as swift as lightning.\n   - 运动员们的速度飞快，竞争异常激烈。 - The athletes\' speed is incredibly swift, and the competition is intense.\n\n4. **Float**\n\nWhen used in specific contexts, "飞" can also mean "float" or "hover" in the air. For example:\n   - 彩纸在风中飞舞。 - The colored paper is floating in the wind.\n   - 热气球在天空中飞翔。 - The hot air balloon is floating in the sky.\n\nIn summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "飞" can include "fly", "flee", "swift", and "float", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
