    summary:
      'The Persian word "وقفه" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Pause, Break\n\nThe most common translation of "وقفه" is "pause" or "break" when referring to a temporary stop or interruption in an activity. For example:\nاو یک وقفه کوتاه برای نفس عمیق گرفت. - He took a short pause to take a deep breath.\nاو برای یک وقفه غذا خورد. - He took a break to have a meal.\n\n## 2. Stop\n\n"وقفه" can also mean "stop" when referring to halting an action or movement. For example:\nوی به زد و خورد بغلی وقفه کرد. - He halted for a moment after the exchange of blows.\nما چند دقیقه در اینجا وقفه کردیم. - We stopped here for a few minutes.\n\n## 3. Rest, Intermission\n\nIn certain contexts, "وقفه" can imply "rest" or "intermission" when referring to a break between two activities. For example:\nاین استارتویل یک وقفه عالی برای نویدیه بود. - The start-up was a great intermission for the newcomer.\nپس از قطعی او به وقفه کوتاهی احتیاج داشت. - After the speech, he needed a short rest.\n\n## 4. Halt\n\nWhen used as a verb, "وقفه" can mean "to halt" or "to come to a stop". For example:\nاو به تکیه زدن به یکی از دسته‌های قرمز وقفه داد. - He halted by leaning on one of the red posts.\nخزندگان به غذارکنی خود وقفه دادند. - The deer halted to feed.\n\nSo in summary, the English translations of the Persian word "وقفه" can include "pause/break", "stop/halt", "rest/intermission", and "halt", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
