    summary:
      'The Chinese character "志" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Ambition, Will\n\nThe most common translation of "志" is "ambition" or "will" when referring to someone\'s goals or aspirations. For example:\n他的志向是成为一名科学家。- His ambition is to become a scientist.\n她有一个坚定的志愿帮助需要帮助的人。- She has a strong will to help those in need.\n\n## 2. Record, Journal\n\n"志" can also mean "record" or "journal" when describing a written account of events or thoughts. For example:\n这本志记录了整个项目的进展。- This journal records the progress of the entire project.\n他在日志中详细描述了他的旅行经历。- He detailed his travel experiences in his journal.\n\n## 3. Spirit, Mind\n\nIn certain contexts, "志" can represent "spirit" or "mind" when referring to one\'s state of mind or determination. For example:\n他们的团结和斗志使他们成功地完成了任务。- Their unity and spirit enabled them to successfully complete the mission.\n她有一颗乐观的志气，总是能够克服困难。- She has an optimistic spirit and can always overcome difficulties.\n\n## 4. Significance\n\nWhen used in a broader sense, "志" can also imply "significance" or "meaning" in certain contexts. For example:\n这个决定对我们的未来发展至关重要。- This decision is of great significance to our future development.\n他们的行动背后有着深刻的志意。- There is profound meaning behind their actions.\n\nIn summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "志" include "ambition/will", "record/journal", "spirit/mind", and "significance/meaning", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
