    summary:
      'The Japanese character "で" has several meanings and functions in the language:\n\n## 1. Particle "de"\n\nOne of the most common uses of "で" is as a particle that indicates the means or method by which an action is performed. For example:\n電車で学校に行きます。- I go to school by train.\n\n## 2. Particle "de" indicating location\n\n"で" can also be used as a particle to indicate the location where an action takes place. For example:\n公園で遊びます。- I play in the park.\n\n## 3. Particle "de" indicating a range or condition\n\nIn some cases, "で" can indicate a range or condition under which something happens. For example:\n30度で涼しいです。- It\'s cool at 30 degrees.\n\n## 4. Particle "de" indicating the means of a state\n\n"で" can also be used to indicate the means by which a certain state or condition is achieved. For example:\n元気で過ごしています。- I am spending my time in good health.\n\nThese are some of the common usages of the Japanese character "で" as a particle in the language.',
