    summary:
      'The Chinese character "近" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Near\n\nThe most common translation of "近" is "near" when referring to proximity or closeness. For example:\n学校很近。 - The school is very near.\n这个地方离火车站很近。 - This place is very close to the train station.\n\n## 2. Recent\n\n"近" can also mean "recent" when describing something that happened or was done not long ago. For example:\n最近的新闻 - Recent news\n他近期怎么样？- How has he been recently?\n\n## 3. Similar to\n\nIn certain contexts, "近" can be used in expressions to mean "similar to" or "close to" in terms of comparison. For example:\n这个问题近于无解。- This problem is close to being unsolvable.\n他的表现近乎完美。- His performance is close to perfection.\n\n## 4. Almost\n\nWhen used in certain phrases, "近" can also convey the meaning of "almost" or "nearly". For example:\n他们已经赢得了近十场比赛。- They have won almost ten games.\n这次活动近满员。- This event is almost full.\n\nIn summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "近" can include "near", "recent", "similar to", and "almost", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
