      'The Portuguese word "instaurar" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Establish, Institute\n\nThe most common translation of "instaurar" is "establish" or "institute" when referring to setting up or creating something new. For example:\nO governo decidiu instaurar novas medidas de segurança. - The government decided to establish new security measures.\nFoi instaurado um comité para investigar o incidente. - A committee was instituted to investigate the incident.\n\n## 2. Restore, Reinstate\n\n"Instaurar" can also mean "restore" or "reinstate" when referring to bringing something back to its previous state. For example:\nEssas reformas visam instaurar a harmonia na sociedade. - These reforms aim to restore harmony in society.\nO juiz decidiu instaurar os direitos do cidadão. - The judge decided to reinstate the citizen\'s rights.\n\n## 3. Initiate, Begin\n\nIn certain contexts, "instaurar" can mean "initiate" or "begin" when referring to starting a process or action. For example:\nA campanha para instaurar novas normas começou ontem. - The campaign to initiate new rules began yesterday.\nO processo de instaurar uma revisão está em andamento. - The process of initiating a review is ongoing.\n\n## 4. Enforce\n\nSometimes "instaurar" can be translated as "enforce" when referring to the implementation or enforcement of rules, laws, or regulations. For example:\nO governo instaurou uma nova política de imigração. - The government enforced a new immigration policy.\nAs autoridades instauraram medidas para garantir a segurança do evento. - Authorities enforced measures to ensure the event\'s security.\n\nIn summary, the English translations of the Portuguese word "instaurar" can include "establish/institute", "restore/reinstate", "initiate/begin", and "enforce", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
