    summary:
      'The Chinese character "比" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Comparison\n\nOne of the main meanings of "比" is "comparison" when used in sentences like:\n这个苹果比那个大。- This apple is bigger than that one.\n\n## 2. Ratio\n\n"比" can also refer to "ratio" or "proportion" in mathematical or quantitative contexts. For example:\n男女比例 - Gender ratio\n价格比较 - Price comparison\n\n## 3. To Compare\n\nAs a verb, "比" can mean "to compare" or "to liken". For example:\n比一比 - Compare\n不能比 - Can\'t be compared\n\n## 4. To Surpass\n\nIn some cases, "比" can be translated as "to surpass" when describing superiority or exceeding expectations. For example:\n胜过比输 - To surpass is to win\n比预期更好 - Better than expected\n\nIn summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "比" can include "comparison", "ratio", "to compare", and "to surpass", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
