    summary:
      'The Chinese character "量" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Quantity, Amount\n\nThe most common translation of "量" is "quantity" or "amount" when referring to the measurement or extent of something. For example:\n这块蛋糕的数量太少了。 - The quantity of this cake is too little.\n他们需要增加产量。 - They need to increase the amount of production.\n\n## 2. Measure, Gauge\n\n"量" can also mean "measure" or "gauge" when referring to the act of determining the size, amount, or degree of something. For example:\n使用这种仪器可以精确测量温度。 - This instrument can measure temperature accurately.\n我们需要一个标准的尺来量一下这个木板的长度。 - We need a standard ruler to measure the length of this wooden board.\n\n## 3. Capacity\n\nIn certain contexts, "量" can also refer to "capacity" when describing the maximum amount that something can hold or contain. For example:\n这个杯子的容量是多少？ - What is the capacity of this cup?\n这个仓库的储存量有限。 - The warehouse has limited storage capacity.\n\n## 4. Assess, Estimate\n\n"量" can also mean "assess" or "estimate" when used in the context of evaluating or judging something. For example:\n我们需要量力而行，不要做出草率决定。 - We need to assess the situation and not make hasty decisions.\n我无法准确地量出他的工作能力。 - I can\'t accurately estimate his work ability.\n\nIn summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "量" can include "quantity/amount", "measure/gauge", "capacity", and "assess/estimate", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
