    summary:
      'The Chinese character "激" has several translations in English, depending on the context:\n\n## 1. Stimulate, Excite\n\nThe most common translation of "激" is "stimulate" or "excite" when referring to causing a reaction or feeling. For example:\n这部电影很激动人心。 - This movie is very exciting.\n这种药物能够激发兴奋感。 - This medication can stimulate a feeling of excitement.\n\n## 2. Jet, Spurt\n\n"激" can also mean "jet" or "spurt" when describing a sudden, forceful flow of liquid or gas. For example:\n水从管子里激射而出。 - Water spurts out from the pipe.\n火焰激射向天空。 - Flames jet up into the sky.\n\n## 3. Encourage, Incite\n\nIn certain contexts, "激" can mean "encourage" or "incite" when urging someone to take action. For example:\n他的话语激励了我。 - His words encouraged me.\n这部小说激发了人们的反抗精神。 - This novel incited people\'s spirit of resistance.\n\n## 4. Thrilling, Provocative\n\nWhen used to describe emotions or events, "激" can mean "thrilling" or "provocative". For example:\n比赛过程令人激动。 - The competition process is thrilling.\n这幅画作具有激情。 - This painting is provocative.\n\nSo in summary, the English translations of the Chinese character "激" can include "stimulate/excite", "jet/spurt", "encourage/incite", and "thrilling/provocative", depending on the specific context in which it is used.',
